// G5 OF THE DOGFOOD ROUTE: THE AGENT SESSION HOLDS A PLACEMENT GRANT AND RUNS INSIDE ITS BOUNDS.
//
// Before this module the model TURN held a fabric seat (gunbc.harness.harness_seat) while the agent
// SESSION that issues those turns held nothing: the worker ran as a transient unit whose MemoryMax
// was the instance's ceiling read straight off the deployment. This module is the session's side of
// the one capacity authority (gunbc.design_argument::conformance fabric/compute row): it reserves the session's memory through
// gunbc.compute.host_capacity -- the same ledger, linearization and quiescence-required release law
// compute_provide uses -- from the host's AGENT SESSION pool, a partition separate from the build pool
// so a session never holds the capacity its own builds need (bold-bee-114 ruling 2026-10-03). The
// amount is gunbc.compute.work_class_grant's answer for WorkClassAgentSession, and the unit's
// MemoryMax is that amount through gunbc.compute.unit_bounds.
//
// THE LIFECYCLE IS gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle's, NOT A SECOND ONE (side-chat ruling on #13074,
// NO-LAND at b4d4a42). A ledger encumbrance is durable and quiescence-required -- a term that runs out
// frees nothing -- so every point at which the spawning process can die must leave a state some
// LATER process can resolve. The compute provider's attempt slot already is that machine: a CAS slot
// keyed by the reservation reference, Reserved -> Launching -> Terminal, a temporal trigger while no
// unit can exist and an observational one once it can. The session conforms to it with one ordering
// difference that closes the window the ruling named: the slot is OPENED BEFORE THE RESERVATION, so
// there is no instant at which the ledger holds this reference and no slot names it. A crash after
// opening and before reserving leaves a slot whose release finds nothing to return; a crash anywhere
// after reserving leaves a slot recovery can terminate and release. (gunbc.compute.work_provider_local
// reserves first and opens second, so it still has that window; it is outside this change.)
//
// WHAT RECOVERY READS AND WHEN. session_placement_settle_pass enumerates every slot in the session
// store (gunbc.durable_cas_file_store cas_slot_keys) -- not the workflow ledger, not the placement
// files -- so a slot whose files were never written is still found. The belt runs it once per tick
// BEFORE any new acquisition, which covers controller death and host reboot as well as returned
// failures, because it starts from the store rather than from anything the dead process meant to do.
//
// DECLARED FRONTIER (gunbc.design_argument::consumption), WITH ITS TRIGGER: reviewer, auditor and supervisor sessions still
// start unleased at the instance ceiling. They join WorkClassAgentSession once a session grant row
// (measured session peaks) sizes the class below the ceiling -- at the ceiling, fourteen reviewer
// lanes per head cannot fit a pool sized to the belt's worker count. Vendor providers (claude, codex,
// cursor) run in tmux, whose panes escape any unit's cgroup, so they hold no placement until they
// move into a unit; their attempts read SessionPlacementAbsent, which is the truth.

// THE ROLE SEGMENT OF THE RECORD NAME. Only the worker holds a placement in this change (see the
// frontier above); a role coproduct lands with the second role rather than as a one-arm type.
data session_worker_role: String = "worker"

data session_placement_schema: String = "gunbc.session-placement/v1"

// HOW LONG A SESSION RESERVATION DECLARES IT WILL HOLD. A declaration and not a deadline: the pool's
// release law is quiescence-required, so an elapsed term frees nothing and the seat returns only by
// the release the settlement pass performs. Four hours is the longest worker the belt has run on
// srv2 with margin.
//
// IT IS A Nat OF SECONDS BECAUSE THAT IS THE POOL'S OWN DURATION CARRIER: product.capacity.pool_events
// SeatRequest.term_seconds and product.capacity.lease LeasePolicy.maximum_duration_seconds are Nat
// seconds, and gunbc.compute.host_capacity host_capacity_reserve takes the term in that form. A
// branded std.types Seconds here would be a second representation cast back to Nat at the call --
// moving the duration onto a typed carrier is a change to the capacity authority's signature, not
// to this consumer (review 74593).
//
// feature:capacity-duration-carrier -- tracked debt, not a settled shape (review 74749).
// dissolve-on: product.capacity.pool_events SeatRequest.term_seconds, product.capacity.lease
// LeasePolicy.maximum_duration_seconds and gunbc.compute.host_capacity host_capacity_reserve's
// term_seconds take a std.measure duration carrier instead of a Nat of seconds. SUFFICIENT FOR
// retyping this row (and compute_reservation_term_seconds, its compute twin) in the same change; until
// then this row stays in the carrier its only consumer accepts. The lease's two instants are already
// carried as EpochSecs (SessionPlacementRecord.granted_at / expires_at), so they are not part of it.
data session_placement_term_seconds: Nat = 14400

// THE SESSION POOL'S SLOTS ARE THE BELT'S WORKER COUNT FOR THAT INSTANCE, derived from it rather than
// chosen (and never a hand-written number -- gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate): the belt already admits at most the instance's
// belt_max_concurrent workers, so a pool of that many ceilings refuses only for memory the machine lacks,
// never for a count launch admission did not impose. Because slots come from the SAME per-instance figure,
// the pool's appropriation (dispatch_worker_memory_max x slots, host_capacity_pool_appropriation) follows
// automatically. srv1-live gets belt_max_concurrent_default slots; the srv1 lab gets srv1_lab_belt_max_concurrent.
fn session_placement_pool(instance: HostDashboardInstance) -> HostCapacityPool {
  // slots is a Nat and belt_max_concurrent is now a Nat too -- the assignment is direct, and there is no
  // "not a natural number" case to refuse: a worker count has no negative representative to reject.
  AgentSessionPool { slots: instance.belt_max_concurrent }
}

// ── THE BINDING: WHICH ATTEMPT, WHICH UNIT, WHICH HOLD ─────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The slot's key and the ledger's reference are the attempt's UNIT NAME, which the dispatch actuator
// derives from the node and the content-hash attempt key -- so one attempt names one hold and two
// attempts never share one. The slot's identity field carries the node and attempt it binds, so a
// record read back is checked against the attempt that is asking rather than trusted because of
// where it was found (ruling, finding 3).
fn session_attempt_identity(node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> String {
  join([node_id, ":", attempt_key], "")
}

fn session_unit(node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> SystemdUnitNameAdmission {
  dispatch_attempt_unit_name(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
}

fn session_unit_wire(node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> NonEmptyStr? {
  match session_unit(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    SystemdUnitNameAdmitted { name } => Present { value: systemd_unit_name_wire(name: name) }
    SystemdUnitNameStemEmpty => none
    SystemdUnitNameDisallowedCharacter { stem: _, character: _ } => none
    SystemdUnitNameOverlong { length: _ } => none
  }
}

fn session_unit_unnameable_detail(node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> String {
  systemd_unit_name_refusal_detail(admission: session_unit(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key))
}

// THE BINDING CHECK, ONE FOLD FOR EVERY READER. A slot is this attempt's only if its reference, its
// unit and its identity all name the same attempt; a mismatch is FOREIGN, and a foreign slot is never
// released by anyone reading it under this attempt's name.
fn session_slot_binding_mismatch(record: AttemptRecord, node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> String {
  match session_unit_wire(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    Absent => session_unit_unnameable_detail(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
    Present { value: expected_unit } => {
  let expected = expected_unit as String
  if record.reference != expected {
    join(["the slot's reference is ", record.reference, " and this attempt's unit is ", expected], "")
  } else if record.unit != expected {
    join(["the slot's unit is ", record.unit, " and this attempt's unit is ", expected], "")
  } else if record.identity != session_attempt_identity(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    join(["the slot binds ", record.identity, " and this attempt is ", session_attempt_identity(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)], "")
  } else {
    ""
  }
    }
  }
}

// THE IDENTITY PARSED BACK, for the settlement pass, which starts from a slot and must find the
// attempt it binds. The attempt key is a hex digest and carries no ':', so the LAST ':' splits.
type SessionAttemptName {
  node_id: String
  attempt_key: String
}

fn session_attempt_name_of(identity: String) -> SessionAttemptName? {
  let parts: List<String> = identity.split(delimiter: ":")
  if count(parts) < 2 { none } else {
    let key = match first(skip(parts, count(parts) - 1)) { Absent => ""  Present { value: p } => p }
    let node = join(parts |> take(count(parts) - 1), ":")
    if key == "" || node == "" { none } else { Present { value: SessionAttemptName { node_id: node, attempt_key: key } } }
  }
}

// ── THE STORES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// WHERE A SESSION'S DURABLE FACTS LIVE, resolved once from the instance and then passed as a value,
// so the settlement pass and its witnesses run the same fold over any store (the compute recovery
// door's own row names an instance-derived root as what kept its control unwritable).
// `slots` is the sealed session slot store (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_root): it is
// minted from an observation of its declared directory and carries no root. `records_dir` is NOT a slot
// store and stays a path: the placement, release and note files under it are plain JSON overwrites, not
// generation-checked slots (the realization census row storage_hand_exclusion for
// session_placement_record_write), so sealing it would be a second store type over a mechanism that
// should itself move onto the slot store; that move changes the records' durable form and is its own change.
// THE STORES THE PASS READS, and the appropriation the ledger was minted with. The appropriation travels
// because reading the ledger's acquisition instant for a reference needs the same pool root the ledger was
// folded with; it is the subject's real appropriation, not a number minted at the read.
type SessionPlacementStores {
  slots: SessionAttemptSlotsStore
  records_dir: String
  store: FabricStorageBinding
  partition: PartitionId
}

type SessionStoresResolution
  = SessionStoresResolved { stores: SessionPlacementStores }
  | SessionStoresUnresolved { detail: String }

fn session_placement_records_dir(instance: HostDashboardInstance) -> String {
  dashboard_instance_dispatch_attempt_state_root(instance: instance) as String
}

fn session_placement_stores(instance: HostDashboardInstance) -> SessionStoresResolution {
  let pool = session_placement_pool(instance: instance)
  match host_capacity_subject(instance: instance, pool: pool) {
        ComputeSubjectHostUnresolved { host } => SessionStoresUnresolved { detail: join(["no dashboard instance is declared for host ", host as String, ", so it has no session ledger"], "") }
        ComputeSubjectResolved { subject, appropriation: _ } =>
          match session_attempt_slots_store(instance: instance) {
            SessionAttemptSlotsStoreUnready { detail } => SessionStoresUnresolved { detail: detail }
            SessionAttemptSlotsStoreReady { store: slots } =>
              // THE LEDGER ARRIVES AS A STANDING. An unstanding ledger is an unresolved store set -- the
              // evidence and settle readers already carry a SessionStoresUnresolved path, so no default
              // store is invented and no seat is freed on a store nobody opened.
              match compute_capacity_store(subject: subject) {
                ComputeCapacityStoreUnready { area: area, detail: detail } => SessionStoresUnresolved { detail: join(["the capacity ledger is not standing at ", area, ": ", detail], "") }
                ComputeCapacityStoreReady { store: ledger } => SessionStoresResolved { stores: SessionPlacementStores {
                  slots: slots,
                  records_dir: session_placement_records_dir(instance: instance),
                  store: ledger,
                  partition: subject.partition,
                } }
              }
          }
      }
}

// ── ACQUISITION: SLOT FIRST, THEN THE LEDGER ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
type SessionPlacementGrant {
  node_id: String
  attempt_key: String
  unit: NonEmptyStr
  lease: LeaseGrant
  partition: PartitionId
  amount: Kibibyte
  class_grant: WorkClassGrant
  slot: AttemptRecord
  slot_generation: CasGeneration
}

type SessionPlacementAcquisition
  = SessionPlacementGranted { grant: SessionPlacementGrant }
  | SessionPlacementRefused { detail: String }

// THE DECLARED WINDOW IS THE CEILING'S OWN ROW, the same as the compute provider's: what it covers is
// the worktree add, the attempt state and the unit's argv -- the steps between acquisition and
// session_placement_begin_launch.
fn session_attempt_record(node_id: String, attempt_key: String, unit: NonEmptyStr, granted: Kibibyte, now: EpochSecs) -> AttemptRecord {
  AttemptRecord {
    identity: session_attempt_identity(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key),
    reference: unit as String,
    unit: unit as String,
    granted: granted,
    opened_at: now,
    launch_deadline: now + compute_pre_launch_ceiling_seconds,
    state: AttemptReserved,
    owner: DispatchOwned { node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key },
  }
}

fn session_placement_acquire(instance: HostDashboardInstance, stores: SessionPlacementStores, node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> SessionPlacementAcquisition {
  match session_unit(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    SystemdUnitNameStemEmpty =>
      SessionPlacementRefused { detail: systemd_unit_name_refusal_detail(admission: SystemdUnitNameStemEmpty) }
    SystemdUnitNameDisallowedCharacter { stem: s, character: ch } =>
      SessionPlacementRefused { detail: systemd_unit_name_refusal_detail(admission: SystemdUnitNameDisallowedCharacter { stem: s, character: ch }) }
    SystemdUnitNameOverlong { length: n } =>
      SessionPlacementRefused { detail: systemd_unit_name_refusal_detail(admission: SystemdUnitNameOverlong { length: n }) }
    SystemdUnitNameAdmitted { name } =>
  {
    let pool = session_placement_pool(instance: instance)
    {
      let class_grant = work_class_grant(class: WorkClassAgentSession, rows: work_class_grant_rows, ceiling: host_capacity_session_seat_ceiling(instance: instance))
      match now_epoch_seconds() {
        Absent => SessionPlacementRefused { detail: "the host clock could not be read as epoch seconds, and the session's slot carries a launch deadline" }
        Present { value: now } => {
          let record = session_attempt_record(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, unit: systemd_unit_name_wire(name: name), granted: work_class_grant_amount(g: class_grant), now: now)
          match attempt_open(store: stores.slots.slots, record: record) {
            AttemptLostRace { expected: e, observed: o } =>
              SessionPlacementRefused { detail: join(["a session slot already exists for ", record.unit, " (expected ", e, ", found ", o, "); one attempt holds at most one placement"], "") }
            AttemptTransitionRefused { detail: d } =>
              SessionPlacementRefused { detail: join(["the session slot could not be opened, so nothing was reserved: ", d], "") }
            AttemptAdvanced { state: _, generation: g } =>
              match host_capacity_reserve(instance: instance, pool: pool, reference: record.unit as NonEmptyStr, term_seconds: session_placement_term_seconds, request: record.granted) {
                ComputeReserved { grant: lease, partition: p, amount: a, store: _ } =>
                  SessionPlacementGranted { grant: SessionPlacementGrant {
                    node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, unit: record.unit as NonEmptyStr,
                    lease: lease, partition: p, amount: a, class_grant: class_grant, slot: record, slot_generation: g,
                  } }
                ComputeCapacityFull { wire: w } => session_refused_after_open(stores: stores, record: record, generation: g, refusal: compute_reservation_wire(r: ComputeCapacityFull { wire: w }))
                ComputeHostBelowFloor { requested: rq, available: av } => session_refused_after_open(stores: stores, record: record, generation: g, refusal: compute_reservation_wire(r: ComputeHostBelowFloor { requested: rq, available: av }))
                ComputeReservationRefused { detail: d } => session_refused_after_open(stores: stores, record: record, generation: g, refusal: compute_reservation_wire(r: ComputeReservationRefused { detail: d }))
              }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  }
}

// A REFUSED RESERVATION CLOSES THE SLOT IT OPENED, and if the close itself fails the slot is left
// Reserved -- which settlement terminates after the deadline, releasing nothing because nothing was
// reserved. Both outcomes are carried in the refusal.
fn session_refused_after_open(stores: SessionPlacementStores, record: AttemptRecord, generation: CasGeneration, refusal: String) -> SessionPlacementAcquisition {
  SessionPlacementRefused {
    detail: join([
      refusal, "; session slot ",
      attempt_transition_wire(t: attempt_terminate(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: record.reference as NonEmptyStr, expected: generation, verdict: AttemptRecovered, detail: join(["reservation refused: ", refusal], ""))),
    ], ""),
  }
}

// THE LAUNCH GATE: Reserved -> Launching, called immediately before the unit is started and never
// after. Losing it means settlement terminated this attempt for overrunning its declared window, and
// the unit must not start; the caller abandons what it holds.
type SessionLaunchGate
  = SessionLaunchAdmitted { grant: SessionPlacementGrant }
  | SessionLaunchRefused { detail: String }

fn session_placement_begin_launch(stores: SessionPlacementStores, grant: SessionPlacementGrant) -> SessionLaunchGate {
  match attempt_begin_launch(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: grant.slot.reference as NonEmptyStr, expected: grant.slot_generation) {
    AttemptAdvanced { state: s, generation: g } =>
      SessionLaunchAdmitted { grant: SessionPlacementGrant {
        node_id: grant.node_id, attempt_key: grant.attempt_key, unit: grant.unit, lease: grant.lease, partition: grant.partition,
        amount: grant.amount, class_grant: grant.class_grant,
        slot: attempt_record_with_state(r: grant.slot, state: s),
        slot_generation: g,
      } }
    AttemptLostRace { expected: e, observed: o } => SessionLaunchRefused { detail: join(["the session slot moved before launch (expected ", e, ", found ", o, "); settlement ended this attempt, so its unit is not started"], "") }
    AttemptTransitionRefused { detail: d } => SessionLaunchRefused { detail: join(["the session slot would not take the launch generation: ", d], "") }
  }
}

// A SPAWN THAT DID NOT HAPPEN RETURNS ITS SEAT ONLY THROUGH A SLOT TRANSITION THAT COMMITTED
// (side-chat ruling on #13074 at c6d50f1). The caller may hold a STALE generation: the launch gate
// advances the slot Reserved -> Launching inside the container step, so a unit-start failure arrives
// here with the pre-launch generation. So:
//   - termination from the supplied generation commits -> release;
//   - it loses -> re-read the slot, and
//       Terminal  -> settlement already closed it; an idempotent release is allowed,
//       Reserved  -> terminate at the generation read, release only if that commits,
//       Launching -> observe the unit: ENDED terminates at the generation read and releases;
//                    ACTIVE or UNREADABLE keeps the charge (the launcher failing is not authoritative
//                    unit absence -- the transient unit is retained precisely so its state can be
//                    read), and the settlement pass releases it once the unit is observed ended,
//       unreadable, absent or mis-bound slot -> keep the charge.
// compute_release_on is NEVER reached merely because an attempted close lost.
type SessionAbandonment {
  freed: ComputeRelease?
  detail: String
}

fn session_abandon_release(stores: SessionPlacementStores, grant: SessionPlacementGrant, reason: NonEmptyStr, closed: String) -> SessionAbandonment {
  // THE LEDGER IS THE ROUTE'S, NOT THE GRANT'S. SessionPlacementStores already carries the capacity ledger the
  // route opened (and the settlement path releases through it); the grant used to carry a SECOND handle to the
  // same store, which every holder could point somewhere else -- including a witness handing it a directory it
  // picked. The grant is data about what was granted; the capability to move capacity stays in one place.
  let freed = compute_release_on(store: stores.store, partition: grant.partition, appropriation: session_ledger_fold_ceiling, reference: grant.lease.reference, reason: reason)
  let write = session_placement_release_write(
    records_dir: stores.records_dir, node_id: grant.node_id, attempt_key: grant.attempt_key,
    grant_binding: Present { value: SessionGrantBinding { grant_identity: grant.lease.fence.grant as String, fence_generation: grant.lease.fence.generation } },
    reason: reason, freed: freed)
  SessionAbandonment {
    freed: Present { value: freed },
    detail: join(["session slot ", closed, "; session placement ", session_release_outcome_wire(r: freed), ": ", session_release_detail(r: freed), session_write_note(w: write)], ""),
  }
}

fn session_abandon_kept(why: String) -> SessionAbandonment {
  SessionAbandonment { freed: none, detail: join(["session placement KEPT: ", why], "") }
}

fn session_abandon_terminate_then_release(stores: SessionPlacementStores, grant: SessionPlacementGrant, record: AttemptRecord, generation: CasGeneration, reason: NonEmptyStr, why: String) -> SessionAbandonment {
  match attempt_terminate(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: record.reference as NonEmptyStr, expected: generation, verdict: AttemptRecovered, detail: join([reason as String, "; ", why], "")) {
    AttemptAdvanced { state: s, generation: _ } => session_abandon_release(stores: stores, grant: grant, reason: reason, closed: join(["closed (", attempt_state_wire(s: s), ") after re-reading: ", why], ""))
    AttemptLostRace { expected: e, observed: o } => session_abandon_kept(why: join(["the slot moved again (expected ", e, ", found ", o, "); the settlement pass decides it from the store"], ""))
    AttemptTransitionRefused { detail: d } => session_abandon_kept(why: join(["the slot would not take the terminal generation: ", d], ""))
  }
}

fn session_placement_abandon_at(stores: SessionPlacementStores, grant: SessionPlacementGrant, reason: NonEmptyStr, lifecycle_of: fn(NonEmptyStr) -> UnitLifecycle) -> SessionAbandonment {
  match attempt_terminate(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: grant.slot.reference as NonEmptyStr, expected: grant.slot_generation, verdict: AttemptRecovered, detail: reason as String) {
    AttemptAdvanced { state: s, generation: _ } => session_abandon_release(stores: stores, grant: grant, reason: reason, closed: join(["closed (", attempt_state_wire(s: s), ")"], ""))
    AttemptTransitionRefused { detail: d } => session_abandon_kept(why: join(["the slot would not take the terminal generation (", d, "); the settlement pass decides it from the store"], ""))
    AttemptLostRace { expected: _, observed: _ } =>
      match attempt_slot_read(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: grant.unit) {
        AttemptSlotUnreadable { detail } => session_abandon_kept(why: join(["the slot close lost and the slot is now unreadable: ", detail], ""))
        AttemptSlotAbsent => session_abandon_kept(why: "the slot close lost and no slot is held under this unit")
        AttemptSlotHeld { record: rec, generation: g } => {
          let mismatch = session_slot_binding_mismatch(record: rec, node_id: grant.node_id, attempt_key: grant.attempt_key)
          if mismatch != "" {
            session_abandon_kept(why: join(["the slot re-read is not this attempt's (", mismatch, ")"], ""))
          } else {
            match rec.state {
              AttemptTerminal { verdict: _, detail: d } => session_abandon_release(stores: stores, grant: grant, reason: reason, closed: join(["already closed (", d, ")"], ""))
              AttemptReserved => session_abandon_terminate_then_release(stores: stores, grant: grant, record: rec, generation: g, reason: reason, why: "the slot is still Reserved")
              AttemptLaunching => {
                let lifecycle = lifecycle_of(grant.unit)
                match lifecycle {
                  UnitTerminatedSuccess { detail: _ } => session_abandon_terminate_then_release(stores: stores, grant: grant, record: rec, generation: g, reason: reason, why: join(["the unit is ", unit_lifecycle_wire(u: lifecycle)], ""))
                  UnitTerminatedFailure { detail: _ } => session_abandon_terminate_then_release(stores: stores, grant: grant, record: rec, generation: g, reason: reason, why: join(["the unit is ", unit_lifecycle_wire(u: lifecycle)], ""))
                  UnitTerminatedCauseUnknown { detail: _ } => session_abandon_terminate_then_release(stores: stores, grant: grant, record: rec, generation: g, reason: reason, why: join(["the unit is ", unit_lifecycle_wire(u: lifecycle)], ""))
                  UnitStillRunning { detail: _ } => session_abandon_kept(why: join(["the slot is Launching and the unit is ", unit_lifecycle_wire(u: lifecycle), "; the settlement pass releases it once the unit is observed ended"], ""))
                  UnitLifecycleUnknown { detail: _ } => session_abandon_kept(why: join(["the slot is Launching and the unit is ", unit_lifecycle_wire(u: lifecycle), "; the settlement pass releases it once the unit is observed ended"], ""))
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
  }
}

fn session_placement_abandon(stores: SessionPlacementStores, grant: SessionPlacementGrant, reason: NonEmptyStr) -> String {
  // THE ABANDONMENT ROUTE HOLDS THE IDENTITY, so it reads its own placement record and hands the reader
  // the launch fact: the grant names the node and attempt key, and that is the key the record is filed
  // under. Nothing here turns a unit name back into an identity.
  (session_placement_abandon_at(
    stores: stores,
    grant: grant,
    reason: reason,
    lifecycle_of: u => session_observe_unit_lifecycle(
      stores: stores,
      unit: u,
      recorded: session_recorded_launch_manager(stores: stores, node_id: grant.node_id, attempt_key: grant.attempt_key),
    ),
  )).detail
}

// ── THE DURABLE PLACEMENT RECORD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The slot is the lifecycle authority; this record is the placement's DESCRIPTION -- the lease
// identity and fence, the partition, the class grant and the unit properties actually passed to
// systemd-run -- written after the reservation and before the launch gate. It names its schema, its
// node, its attempt, its host and its unit, and the reader refuses it unless every one of them is
// the asking attempt's (ruling, finding 3).
fn session_placement_record_basename(node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> String {
  join(["session-placement-", node_id, "-a", attempt_key, "-", session_worker_role, ".json"], "")
}

fn session_placement_release_basename(node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> String {
  join(["session-placement-", node_id, "-a", attempt_key, "-", session_worker_role, ".release.json"], "")
}

fn session_placement_note_basename(unit: String) -> String {
  join(["session-placement-note-", unit, ".txt"], "")
}

type SessionPlacementRecord {
  schema: String
  node_id: String
  attempt_key: String
  host: String
  unit: String
  reference: String
  grant_identity: String
  fence_generation: CasGeneration
  granted_at: EpochSecs
  expires_at: EpochSecs
  partition: String
  amount: Kibibyte
  class_grant: String
  launch_manager: SessionRecordedLaunchManager
  unit_properties: List<String>
}

// THE RECORD CARRIES THE LAUNCH FACT. The writer knows the route it launched on -- the session attempt
// route creates its unit with systemd-run on the SYSTEM manager, and there is no --user path -- so the
// route is a parameter the caller states, not something a later reader infers from the unit's name.
fn session_placement_record_of(host: String, grant: SessionPlacementGrant, launch_manager: UnitLaunchManagerRoute, unit_properties: List<String>) -> SessionPlacementRecord {
  SessionPlacementRecord {
    schema: session_placement_schema,
    node_id: grant.node_id,
    attempt_key: grant.attempt_key,
    host: host,
    unit: grant.unit as String,
    reference: grant.lease.reference as String,
    grant_identity: grant.lease.fence.grant as String,
    fence_generation: grant.lease.fence.generation,
    granted_at: grant.lease.granted_at,
    expires_at: grant.lease.expires_at,
    partition: grant.partition as String,
    amount: grant.amount,
    class_grant: work_class_grant_wire(g: grant.class_grant),
    launch_manager: LaunchManagerRecorded { manager: launch_manager },
    unit_properties: unit_properties,
  }
}

// THE launch_manager MEMBER, present only when the record carries the fact. An unrecorded record writes
// NO KEY, so what the decoder answers Unrecorded for stays its own wire form: the round trip of a
// pre-receipt record is byte-honest, and a PRESENT value always names a manager.
fn session_launch_manager_record_member(manager: SessionRecordedLaunchManager) -> List<JsonKeyValue> {
  match manager {
    LaunchManagerRecorded { manager: route } => [json_kv(key: "launch_manager", value: json_string(s: session_launch_manager_wire(route: route)))]
    LaunchManagerUnrecorded => []
  }
}

fn session_placement_record_json(r: SessionPlacementRecord) -> JsonValue {
  json_object(members: concat([
    json_kv(key: "schema", value: json_string(s: r.schema)),
    json_kv(key: "node_id", value: json_string(s: r.node_id)),
    json_kv(key: "attempt_key", value: json_string(s: r.attempt_key)),
    json_kv(key: "host", value: json_string(s: r.host)),
    json_kv(key: "unit", value: json_string(s: r.unit)),
    json_kv(key: "reference", value: json_string(s: r.reference)),
    json_kv(key: "grant_identity", value: json_string(s: r.grant_identity)),
    json_kv(key: "fence_generation", value: json_int(n: cas_generation_count(g: r.fence_generation))),
    json_kv(key: "granted_at", value: json_int(n: r.granted_at)),
    json_kv(key: "expires_at", value: json_int(n: r.expires_at)),
    json_kv(key: "partition", value: json_string(s: r.partition)),
    json_kv(key: "amount_kib", value: json_int(n: kibibyte_count(k: r.amount))),
    json_kv(key: "class_grant", value: json_string(s: r.class_grant)),
  ], concat(session_launch_manager_record_member(manager: r.launch_manager), [
    json_kv(key: "unit_properties", value: json_array(elements: map(r.unit_properties, p => json_string(s: p)))),
  ])))
}

type SessionPlacementWrite
  = SessionPlacementWritten { path: String }
  | SessionPlacementWriteFailed { path: String, error: String }

fn session_write_note(w: SessionPlacementWrite) -> String {
  match w {
    SessionPlacementWritten { path: _ } => ""
    SessionPlacementWriteFailed { path, error } => join([" (record not written at ", path, ": ", error, ")"], "")
  }
}

fn session_placement_record_write(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, grant: SessionPlacementGrant, launch_manager: UnitLaunchManagerRoute, unit_properties: List<String>) -> SessionPlacementWrite {
  let path = join([stores.records_dir, "/", session_placement_record_basename(node_id: grant.node_id, attempt_key: grant.attempt_key)], "")
  let w = Filesystem.Write(path: path, content: serialize_json(v: session_placement_record_json(r: session_placement_record_of(host: host, grant: grant, launch_manager: launch_manager, unit_properties: unit_properties))))
  if w.success { SessionPlacementWritten { path: path } } else { SessionPlacementWriteFailed { path: path, error: w.error } }
}

// ── THE RELEASE RECORD, BOUND TO THE GRANT AND FENCE IT RETURNED ───────────────────────────────
//
// A reference is reusable text; a grant identity and its fence name ONE hold. The release carries
// the hold it returned when the releaser knows it, and says it does not (the `grant` member is
// absent) when settlement released from a slot whose placement record was never written -- in which
// case the reader requires that there IS no placement record to disagree with.
type SessionGrantBinding {
  grant_identity: String
  fence_generation: CasGeneration
}

fn session_release_outcome_wire(r: ComputeRelease) -> String {
  match r {
    ComputeReleased { partition: _, reference: _, reason: _ } => "released"
    ComputeNothingToRelease { detail: _ } => "nothing-to-release"
    ComputeReleaseRefused { detail: _ } => "refused"
  }
}

fn session_release_detail(r: ComputeRelease) -> String {
  match r {
    ComputeReleased { partition: p, reference: rf, reason: rs } => join(["released ", rf as String, " on ", p as String, " (", rs as String, ")"], "")
    ComputeNothingToRelease { detail: d } => d
    ComputeReleaseRefused { detail: d } => d
  }
}

fn session_placement_release_write(records_dir: String, node_id: String, attempt_key: String, grant_binding: SessionGrantBinding?, reason: NonEmptyStr, freed: ComputeRelease) -> SessionPlacementWrite {
  let path = join([records_dir, "/", session_placement_release_basename(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)], "")
  match session_unit_wire(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    Absent => SessionPlacementWriteFailed { path: path, error: session_unit_unnameable_detail(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) }
    Present { value: unit } => {
  let w = Filesystem.Write(path: path, content: serialize_json(v: json_object(members: concat([
    json_kv(key: "schema", value: json_string(s: session_placement_schema)),
    json_kv(key: "node_id", value: json_string(s: node_id)),
    json_kv(key: "attempt_key", value: json_string(s: attempt_key)),
    json_kv(key: "reference", value: json_string(s: unit as String)),
    json_kv(key: "outcome", value: json_string(s: session_release_outcome_wire(r: freed))),
    json_kv(key: "reason", value: json_string(s: reason as String)),
    json_kv(key: "detail", value: json_string(s: session_release_detail(r: freed))),
  ], match grant_binding {
    Absent => []
    Present { value: b } => [json_kv(key: "grant", value: json_object(members: [
      json_kv(key: "grant_identity", value: json_string(s: b.grant_identity)),
      json_kv(key: "fence_generation", value: json_int(n: cas_generation_count(g: b.fence_generation))),
    ]))]
  }))))
  if w.success { SessionPlacementWritten { path: path } } else { SessionPlacementWriteFailed { path: path, error: w.error } }
    }
  }
}

// ── READING THE FILES BACK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
type SessionFieldsAcc {
  record: SessionPlacementRecord?
  cause: String
}

fn session_field_cause<T>(key: String, r: JsonFieldRead<T>) -> String {
  match r {
    FieldAbsent => join([key, " is missing"], "")
    FieldMalformed { cause } => cause
    FieldRead { value: _ } => ""
  }
}

fn session_string_or(r: JsonFieldRead<String>) -> String {
  match r { FieldRead { value } => value  FieldAbsent => ""  FieldMalformed { cause: _ } => "" }
}

fn session_int_or(r: JsonFieldRead<Int>) -> Int {
  match r { FieldRead { value } => value  FieldAbsent => 0  FieldMalformed { cause: _ } => 0 }
}

// AN INSTANT ON THE WIRE IS RE-ADMITTED, NOT CAST (the same rule as gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle
// attempt_member_epoch): a negative number is not an epoch second.
fn session_epoch_cause(key: String, r: JsonFieldRead<Int>) -> String {
  match r {
    FieldRead { value } => if value < 0 { join([key, " is ", to_string(value: value), ", which is not an epoch second"], "") } else { "" }
    FieldAbsent => join([key, " is missing"], "")
    FieldMalformed { cause } => cause
  }
}

fn session_nat_or(r: JsonFieldRead<Nat>) -> Nat {
  match r { FieldRead { value } => value  FieldAbsent => 0  FieldMalformed { cause: _ } => 0 }
}

// WHAT A launch_manager FIELD COSTS THE RECORD. ABSENT COSTS NOTHING, and that is deliberate rather
// than lax: the records written before this field exists must still PARSE, and bumping the schema string
// would turn the two pre-receipt srv1 leases into UNREADABLE records and keep their seats for the wrong
// reason. A PRESENT value that names neither manager fails closed -- a half-named manager is not the
// system one. The fallback in session_launch_manager_or is reached only when this cause is non-empty.
fn session_launch_manager_cause(r: JsonFieldRead<String>) -> String {
  match r {
    FieldAbsent => ""
    FieldRead { value: raw } =>
      if raw == session_launch_manager_wire_system || raw == session_launch_manager_wire_user {
        ""
      } else {
        join(["launch_manager names ", raw, ", which is neither declared manager"], "")
      }
    FieldMalformed { cause: c } => c
  }
}

fn session_launch_manager_or(r: JsonFieldRead<String>) -> SessionRecordedLaunchManager {
  match r {
    FieldRead { value: raw } =>
      if raw == session_launch_manager_wire_user { LaunchManagerRecorded { manager: UnitRunOnUserManager } } else { LaunchManagerRecorded { manager: UnitRunOnSystemManager } }
    FieldAbsent => LaunchManagerUnrecorded
    FieldMalformed { cause: _ } => LaunchManagerUnrecorded
  }
}

// EVERY FIELD IS REQUIRED. The first missing or malformed one is the refusal; the zero and empty
// fallbacks above are reached only when that cause is non-empty, so no record is ever built from them.
// launch_manager is the one field whose ABSENCE is not a cause -- see session_launch_manager_cause.
fn session_placement_record_decode(doc: JsonValue) -> SessionFieldsAcc {
  let schema = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "schema")
  let node_id = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "node_id")
  let attempt_key = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "attempt_key")
  let host = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "host")
  let unit = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "unit")
  let reference = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "reference")
  let grant_identity = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "grant_identity")
  let fence_generation = json_field_nat(obj: doc, key: "fence_generation")
  let granted_at = json_field_int(obj: doc, key: "granted_at")
  let expires_at = json_field_int(obj: doc, key: "expires_at")
  let partition = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "partition")
  let amount_kib = json_field_nat(obj: doc, key: "amount_kib")
  let class_grant = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "class_grant")
  let launch_manager = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "launch_manager")
  let unit_properties = json_field_string_list(obj: doc, key: "unit_properties")
  let causes = filter([
    session_field_cause(key: "schema", r: schema),
    session_field_cause(key: "node_id", r: node_id),
    session_field_cause(key: "attempt_key", r: attempt_key),
    session_field_cause(key: "host", r: host),
    session_field_cause(key: "unit", r: unit),
    session_field_cause(key: "reference", r: reference),
    session_field_cause(key: "grant_identity", r: grant_identity),
    session_field_cause(key: "fence_generation", r: fence_generation),
    match fence_generation {
      FieldRead { value: n } => match cas_generation(n: n as Int) { Absent => "fence_generation is not a granted fence"  Present { value: _ } => "" }
      FieldAbsent => ""
      FieldMalformed { cause: _ } => ""
    },
    session_epoch_cause(key: "granted_at", r: granted_at),
    session_epoch_cause(key: "expires_at", r: expires_at),
    session_field_cause(key: "partition", r: partition),
    session_field_cause(key: "amount_kib", r: amount_kib),
    session_field_cause(key: "class_grant", r: class_grant),
    session_launch_manager_cause(r: launch_manager),
    session_field_cause(key: "unit_properties", r: unit_properties),
  ], c => c != "")
  match causes.first() {
    Present { value: c } => SessionFieldsAcc { record: none, cause: c }
    Absent =>
      SessionFieldsAcc {
        record: Present { value: SessionPlacementRecord {
          schema: session_string_or(r: schema),
          node_id: session_string_or(r: node_id),
          attempt_key: session_string_or(r: attempt_key),
          host: session_string_or(r: host),
          unit: session_string_or(r: unit),
          reference: session_string_or(r: reference),
          grant_identity: session_string_or(r: grant_identity),
          fence_generation: match fence_generation {
            FieldRead { value: n } => match cas_generation(n: n as Int) { Present { value: g } => g  Absent => cas_generation_first() }
            FieldAbsent => cas_generation_first()
            FieldMalformed { cause: _ } => cas_generation_first()
          },
          granted_at: session_int_or(r: granted_at),
          expires_at: session_int_or(r: expires_at),
          partition: session_string_or(r: partition),
          amount: kibibyte(count: session_nat_or(r: amount_kib)),
          class_grant: session_string_or(r: class_grant),
          launch_manager: session_launch_manager_or(r: launch_manager),
          unit_properties: match unit_properties { FieldRead { value } => value  FieldAbsent => []  FieldMalformed { cause: _ } => [] },
        } },
        cause: "",
      }
  }
}

// THE PLACEMENT RECORD'S BINDING, checked against the asking attempt.
fn session_record_binding_mismatch(r: SessionPlacementRecord, node_id: String, attempt_key: String, host: String) -> String {
  match session_unit_wire(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    Absent => session_unit_unnameable_detail(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
    Present { value: expected_unit } => {
  let expected = expected_unit as String
  if r.schema != session_placement_schema {
    join(["the placement record's schema is ", r.schema, ", not ", session_placement_schema], "")
  } else if r.node_id != node_id || r.attempt_key != attempt_key {
    join(["the placement record belongs to ", r.node_id, ":", r.attempt_key, ", not ", node_id, ":", attempt_key], "")
  } else if r.unit != expected || r.reference != expected {
    join(["the placement record names unit ", r.unit, " and reference ", r.reference, "; this attempt's unit is ", expected], "")
  } else if r.host != host {
    join(["the placement record was written on host ", r.host, ", not ", host], "")
  } else {
    ""
  }
    }
  }
}

fn session_file_observation_cause(o: FilesystemFileObservation) -> String {
  match o {
    FilesystemFileAbsent(_) => "absent"
    FilesystemFileRead { path: _, content: _ } => ""
    FilesystemFileIndeterminate { cause } => cause
    FilesystemFileObservationsDisagree { path: _, cause } => cause
    FilesystemFileSubjectRefused { directory: _, name: _, cause } => cause
  }
}

type SessionGrantReading
  = SessionGrantRecorded { record: SessionPlacementRecord }
  | SessionGrantNotRecorded { path: String }
  | SessionGrantUnreadable { path: String, detail: String }
  | SessionGrantForeign { path: String, detail: String }

fn session_grant_reading_of(path: String, obs: FilesystemFileObservation, node_id: String, attempt_key: String, host: String) -> SessionGrantReading {
  match obs {
    FilesystemFileAbsent(_) => SessionGrantNotRecorded { path: path }
    FilesystemFileRead { path: _, content } =>
      match parse_json_document(s: content) {
        JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap } => SessionGrantUnreadable { path: path, detail: json_document_gap_text(gap: gap) }
        JsonDocumentParsed { value: doc } => {
          let decoded = session_placement_record_decode(doc: doc)
          match decoded.record {
            Absent => SessionGrantUnreadable { path: path, detail: decoded.cause }
            Present { value: r } => {
              let mismatch = session_record_binding_mismatch(r: r, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, host: host)
              if mismatch == "" { SessionGrantRecorded { record: r } } else { SessionGrantForeign { path: path, detail: mismatch } }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    FilesystemFileIndeterminate { cause: _ } => SessionGrantUnreadable { path: path, detail: session_file_observation_cause(o: obs) }
    FilesystemFileObservationsDisagree { path: _, cause: _ } => SessionGrantUnreadable { path: path, detail: session_file_observation_cause(o: obs) }
    FilesystemFileSubjectRefused { directory: _, name: _, cause: _ } => SessionGrantUnreadable { path: path, detail: session_file_observation_cause(o: obs) }
  }
}

type SessionReleaseObservation
  = SessionReleaseNotRecorded { path: String }
  | SessionReleased { reason: String, detail: String }
  | SessionReleaseNothingHeld { reason: String, detail: String }
  | SessionReleaseRefused { reason: String, detail: String }
  | SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: String, detail: String }

fn session_release_grant_mismatch(doc: JsonValue, grant: SessionGrantReading) -> String {
  match json_field(obj: doc, key: "grant") {
    FieldMalformed { cause } => cause
    FieldAbsent =>
      match grant {
        SessionGrantRecorded { record } => join(["the release names no grant, and this attempt's placement holds grant ", record.grant_identity], "")
        SessionGrantNotRecorded { path: _ } => ""
        SessionGrantUnreadable { path: _, detail: _ } => ""
        SessionGrantForeign { path: _, detail: d } => d
      }
    FieldRead { value: g } => {
      let identity = session_string_or(r: json_field_string(obj: g, key: "grant_identity"))
      match grant {
        SessionGrantRecorded { record } =>
          match json_field_nat(obj: g, key: "fence_generation") {
            FieldRead { value: f } =>
              if identity != record.grant_identity || (f as Int) != cas_generation_count(g: record.fence_generation) {
                join(["the release returned grant ", identity, " at fence ", to_string(value: f), ", and this attempt's placement holds ", record.grant_identity, " at fence ", to_string(value: cas_generation_count(g: record.fence_generation))], "")
              } else { "" }
            FieldAbsent => "the release's grant carries no fence generation"
            FieldMalformed { cause } => cause
          }
        SessionGrantNotRecorded { path: _ } => ""
        SessionGrantUnreadable { path: _, detail: _ } => ""
        SessionGrantForeign { path: _, detail: d } => d
      }
    }
  }
}

fn session_release_observation_of(path: String, obs: FilesystemFileObservation, node_id: String, attempt_key: String, grant: SessionGrantReading) -> SessionReleaseObservation {
  match obs {
    FilesystemFileAbsent(_) => SessionReleaseNotRecorded { path: path }
    FilesystemFileRead { path: _, content } =>
      match parse_json_document(s: content) {
        JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap } => SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: path, detail: json_document_gap_text(gap: gap) }
        JsonDocumentParsed { value: doc } => {
          let nd = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "node_id")
          let ak = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "attempt_key")
          let rf = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "reference")
          let outcome = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "outcome")
          let reason = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "reason")
          let detail = json_field_string(obj: doc, key: "detail")
          let causes = filter([
            session_field_cause(key: "node_id", r: nd), session_field_cause(key: "attempt_key", r: ak),
            session_field_cause(key: "reference", r: rf), session_field_cause(key: "outcome", r: outcome),
            session_field_cause(key: "reason", r: reason), session_field_cause(key: "detail", r: detail),
          ], c => c != "")
          match causes.first() {
            Present { value: c } => SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: path, detail: c }
            Absent => {
              let admitted_unit = session_unit_wire(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
              let mismatch = if session_string_or(r: nd) != node_id || session_string_or(r: ak) != attempt_key {
                join(["the release belongs to ", session_string_or(r: nd), ":", session_string_or(r: ak), ", not ", node_id, ":", attempt_key], "")
              } else {
                match admitted_unit {
                  Absent => session_unit_unnameable_detail(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
                  Present { value: unit } =>
                    if session_string_or(r: rf) != (unit as String) {
                      join(["the release names reference ", session_string_or(r: rf), ", not this attempt's unit"], "")
                    } else {
                      session_release_grant_mismatch(doc: doc, grant: grant)
                    }
                }
              }
              if mismatch != "" {
                SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: path, detail: mismatch }
              } else if session_string_or(r: outcome) == "released" {
                SessionReleased { reason: session_string_or(r: reason), detail: session_string_or(r: detail) }
              } else if session_string_or(r: outcome) == "nothing-to-release" {
                SessionReleaseNothingHeld { reason: session_string_or(r: reason), detail: session_string_or(r: detail) }
              } else if session_string_or(r: outcome) == "refused" {
                SessionReleaseRefused { reason: session_string_or(r: reason), detail: session_string_or(r: detail) }
              } else {
                SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: path, detail: join(["release outcome is not in the closed vocabulary: ", session_string_or(r: outcome)], "") }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    FilesystemFileIndeterminate { cause: _ } => SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: path, detail: session_file_observation_cause(o: obs) }
    FilesystemFileObservationsDisagree { path: _, cause: _ } => SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: path, detail: session_file_observation_cause(o: obs) }
    FilesystemFileSubjectRefused { directory: _, name: _, cause: _ } => SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: path, detail: session_file_observation_cause(o: obs) }
  }
}

fn session_release_settled(r: SessionReleaseObservation) -> Bool {
  match r {
    SessionReleased { reason: _, detail: _ } => true
    SessionReleaseNothingHeld { reason: _, detail: _ } => true
    SessionReleaseNotRecorded { path: _ } => false
    SessionReleaseRefused { reason: _, detail: _ } => false
    SessionReleaseUnreadable { path: _, detail: _ } => false
  }
}

// ── THE READER THE DOGFOOD RECEIPT FOLD CALLS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// CLOSED, AND NO ARM IS A DEFAULT. It takes the asking attempt's node and key and derives the unit,
// so it reads THIS attempt's slot by key and checks every file it reads against the attempt it is
// asking about: a slot, record or release belonging to another attempt reads FOREIGN, never Observed.
type SessionPlacementObservation
  = SessionPlacementObserved { slot: AttemptRecord, grant: SessionGrantReading, returned: SessionReleaseObservation }
  | SessionPlacementAbsent { unit: String }
  | SessionPlacementUnreadable { unit: String, detail: String }
  | SessionPlacementForeign { unit: String, detail: String }
  | SessionPlacementUnnameable { detail: String }

// THE PURE FOLD over what the caller read, so witnesses supply planted readings and the reader below
// supplies real ones.
fn session_placement_observation_of(
  node_id: String, attempt_key: String, host: String,
  slot: AttemptSlotReading,
  record_path: String, record: FilesystemFileObservation,
  release_path: String, released: FilesystemFileObservation,
) -> SessionPlacementObservation {
  match session_unit_wire(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    Absent => SessionPlacementUnnameable {
      detail: session_unit_unnameable_detail(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key),
    }
    Present { value: named } => {
  let unit = named as String
  match slot {
    AttemptSlotAbsent => SessionPlacementAbsent { unit: unit }
    AttemptSlotUnreadable { detail } => SessionPlacementUnreadable { unit: unit, detail: detail }
    AttemptSlotHeld { record: rec, generation: _ } => {
      let mismatch = session_slot_binding_mismatch(record: rec, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
      if mismatch != "" {
        SessionPlacementForeign { unit: unit, detail: mismatch }
      } else {
        let grant = session_grant_reading_of(path: record_path, obs: record, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, host: host)
        match grant {
          SessionGrantForeign { path: _, detail } => SessionPlacementForeign { unit: unit, detail: detail }
          SessionGrantRecorded { record: _ } => SessionPlacementObserved { slot: rec, grant: grant, returned: session_release_observation_of(path: release_path, obs: released, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, grant: grant) }
          SessionGrantNotRecorded { path: _ } => SessionPlacementObserved { slot: rec, grant: grant, returned: session_release_observation_of(path: release_path, obs: released, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, grant: grant) }
          SessionGrantUnreadable { path: _, detail: _ } => SessionPlacementObserved { slot: rec, grant: grant, returned: session_release_observation_of(path: release_path, obs: released, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, grant: grant) }
        }
      }
    }
  }
    }
  }
}

fn session_placement_file(dir: String, name: String) -> FilesystemFileObservation {
  let path = join([dir, "/", name], "")
  let listing = Filesystem.List(path: dir)
  let read = Filesystem.Read(path: path)
  filesystem_file_observation(
    listing: filesystem_listing_observation(directory: dir, success: listing.success, entries: listing.entries, error: listing.error),
    name: name,
    path: path,
    read: filesystem_read_outcome(content: read.content, success: read.success, error: read.error),
  )
}

fn session_placement_observe_at(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> SessionPlacementObservation {
  match session_unit_wire(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    Absent => SessionPlacementUnnameable {
      detail: session_unit_unnameable_detail(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key),
    }
    Present { value: unit } => {
  let record_name = session_placement_record_basename(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
  let release_name = session_placement_release_basename(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
  session_placement_observation_of(
    node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, host: host,
    slot: attempt_slot_read(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: unit),
    record_path: join([stores.records_dir, "/", record_name], ""), record: session_placement_file(dir: stores.records_dir, name: record_name),
    release_path: join([stores.records_dir, "/", release_name], ""), released: session_placement_file(dir: stores.records_dir, name: release_name),
  )
    }
  }
}

// THE STAGE READER: the worker session's slot (its lifecycle), its grant (identity, fence, unit
// properties applied) and its release, for THIS node's THIS attempt.
fn session_placement_observe_for_attempt(instance: HostDashboardInstance, node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> SessionPlacementObservation {
  match session_unit_wire(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    Absent => SessionPlacementUnnameable {
      detail: session_unit_unnameable_detail(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key),
    }
    Present { value: unit } =>
  match session_placement_stores(instance: instance) {
    SessionStoresUnresolved { detail } => SessionPlacementUnreadable { unit: unit as String, detail: detail }
    SessionStoresResolved { stores } => session_placement_observe_at(stores: stores, host: instance.host_identity as String, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
  }
  }
}

// ── SETTLEMENT: THE INDEPENDENT PASS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// THE UNIT'S LIFECYCLE IN THE AUTHORITY'S FIVE ARMS, from the worker's own observation (the read the
// belt already makes for liveness). A unit the manager does not have is ended with cause unknown --
// the one arm safe to free on without a verdict; an exited unit is ended with its status; an
// unreadable manager is UNKNOWN and frees nothing.
// ── THE HOLDER'S IDENTITY, FOR THE ARMS THAT FREE A SEAT ON A UNIT THE MANAGER NO LONGER HAS ───
//
// A transient unit is COLLECTED when its process ends, so "the manager has no unit by that name" is the
// ordinary state of a unit that ran and finished -- and equally the state of one whose manager
// restarted. Neither reading is proof of death on its own. The recurring-failure-mode row
// gunbc.recurring_failure_mode hold_recovered_by_age_not_observed_holder_death names this shape: a hold
// recovered because the evidence was old, not because the holder was observed dead. What binds a
// not-found reading to the holder is the identity the manager keeps -- the InvocationID of the run --
// together with the boot the manager and the unit lived in, ordered against the instant the LEDGER
// acquired the seat. The acquisition instant comes from the ledger, not from the slot's opened_at: a
// slot that has already been advanced carries the instant of its own last write, not the instant the
// seat was taken.
//
// THE SKEW IS A DECLARED VALUE AT THE READER, not a number a caller may pass. btime and the ledger's
// acquired_at are both whole seconds of the host clock read at different moments, and a clock set from
// the RTC before synchronization can put them apart by more than a second. This reader answers within
// 120 seconds; anything closer is a typed refusal, never a rounding.
data session_holder_boot_skew_bound_seconds: Seconds = 120

// ── WHO MAY BE READ AS A HOLDER: THE RECORDED LAUNCH MANAGER ──────────────────────────────────
//
// WHAT MANAGER RAN A SESSION ATTEMPT'S UNIT IS A LAUNCH FACT, AND THE LAUNCH KNOWS IT: the session
// attempt route creates its unit with systemd-run on the SYSTEM manager (roadmap_dispatch_actuator
// attempt_system_unit_launch has no --user path), so the writer records the route into the placement
// record at the moment it writes the record. ADMISSIBILITY IS THAT FACT'S CALL, NOT THE NAME'S. The
// prefix rule (roadmap_attempt_occurrence occurrence_unit_launch_manager_route) still says which
// manager a READING was taken from -- that is what makes a standing about one manager unable to speak
// for a unit launched on another -- but it no longer decides which placement a reading may be admitted
// for. That distinction is the root of the srv1 wedges: a lease whose unit name was claimed by nothing
// (or by the wrong manager) kept its seat through the NAME, and no recorded fact could say otherwise.
// (Branch review 2026-11-07, mgr ruling msg_2b3b7c0c.)
//
// THE MANAGER VOCABULARY IS THE ONE ALREADY DECLARED (roadmap_attempt_occurrence
// UnitLaunchManagerRoute); this module mints no second manager coproduct.
type SessionRecordedLaunchManager
  = LaunchManagerRecorded { manager: UnitLaunchManagerRoute }
  | LaunchManagerUnrecorded

// WHAT READING THE RECORD GIVES. UNREADABLE IS ITS OWN ARM because a record that could not be read,
// parsed or bound is not a record that omits the field: the first is a fact the reader does not have,
// the second is a fact the launch did not record, and only the second may reach the legacy list.
type SessionLaunchManagerReading
  = LaunchManagerRead { manager: SessionRecordedLaunchManager }
  | LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: String }

data session_launch_manager_wire_system: String = "system"
data session_launch_manager_wire_user: String = "user"

// THE ONLY RECORDS ADMITTED WITHOUT THE RECORDED FACT, listed BY VALUE for exactly the two srv1 leases
// that predate the receipt (leases acquired Oct 14 and Oct 28 2026, before any launch manager was
// written). Everything else that carries no recorded manager keeps its slot and says so.
//
// WHY THESE TWO AND NO OTHERS: they are the two lease references named in the hand-off (spec
// msg_05e6741a) -- the srv1 leases whose placement records were written before this field existed, which
// is exactly the population this arm exists for. This is a LIST OF VALUES, not a claim about what any
// host holds: no control in this change reads srv1. And its incompleteness FAILS CLOSED -- a record
// without the field that is NOT listed keeps its slot and is refused by name, which is the same shape
// the wedge had before, but now with the missing fact stated instead of a name prefix guessing. A
// record written after this change carries the field; a record that cannot be read at all is
// LaunchManagerUnreadable and never reaches this list.
//
// CARRIED HERE AND NOT IN A CENSUS ROW, and its retirement condition: dag/gunbc/realization_census_rows
// .dag is a REGENERATED artifact (rows_gen from a pinned receipt; its own header forbids editing), so a
// hand-added row there would be erased by the next regeneration. RETIRE THIS ROW BY EMPTYING IT: once
// both references are settled, or re-acquired with a recorded manager, the legacy arm has no members,
// the list is empty, and the row and the Legacy arm go with it.
data session_legacy_recorded_manager_absent_references: List<String> = [
  "gunbc-attempt-debt-exclusion-frontier-excludes-nothing-6ea61c671002a6d4.service",
  "gunbc-attempt-v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority-25de491353dd507f.service",
]

// THE ADMISSION ANSWER. Refused names WHICH FACT IS MISSING; Legacy is admitted and LABELLED, so an
// admitted-without-the-receipt lease is distinguishable in the witness and in the refusal text from one
// admitted on its record.
type SessionManagerAdmission
  = ManagerAdmissionGranted { manager: UnitLaunchManagerRoute }
  | ManagerAdmissionLegacy { reference: NonEmptyStr }
  | ManagerAdmissionRefused { detail: String }

fn session_launch_manager_wire(route: UnitLaunchManagerRoute) -> String {
  match route {
    UnitRunOnSystemManager => session_launch_manager_wire_system
    UnitRunOnUserManager => session_launch_manager_wire_user
  }
}

// THE ADMISSIBILITY DECISION, in one place: the manager RECORDED on the placement record against the
// manager the READER actually took its reading from, with the legacy list as the only route admitted
// without the recorded fact. A mismatch refuses naming BOTH -- that is the pair the old prefix rule
// collapsed into one name, and it is how a reading taken from the wrong manager would otherwise come to
// look like evidence about the holder.
fn session_launch_manager_admissible(
  reading: SessionLaunchManagerReading,
  route: UnitLaunchManagerRoute?,
  reference: NonEmptyStr,
) -> SessionManagerAdmission {
  match route {
    Absent => ManagerAdmissionRefused {
      detail: join(["no launcher in the corpus claims a unit named ", reference as String, ", so no manager is declared for it; guessing one would manufacture a death reading taken from the wrong manager"], ""),
    }
    Present { value: observed } => match reading {
      LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail } => ManagerAdmissionRefused {
        detail: join(["the placement record for ", reference as String, " could not be read to say which manager launched it: ", detail], ""),
      }
      LaunchManagerRead { manager: LaunchManagerRecorded { manager: recorded } } =>
        if session_launch_manager_wire(route: recorded) == session_launch_manager_wire(route: observed) {
          ManagerAdmissionGranted { manager: recorded }
        } else {
          ManagerAdmissionRefused {
            detail: join(["the placement record launched ", reference as String, " on the ", session_launch_manager_wire(route: recorded), " manager, and the reading was taken on the ", session_launch_manager_wire(route: observed), " manager: two managers' answers are not one holder"], ""),
          }
        }
      LaunchManagerRead { manager: LaunchManagerUnrecorded } =>
        if any(session_legacy_recorded_manager_absent_references, r => r == (reference as String)) {
          ManagerAdmissionLegacy { reference: reference }
        } else {
          ManagerAdmissionRefused {
            detail: join(["no launch manager recorded on the placement record for ", reference as String, ", and the reference is not on the legacy list"], ""),
          }
        }
    }
  }
}

// WHICH RECORD FILE CARRIES THE FACT, keyed by the IDENTITY THE CALLER HOLDS. Nothing here derives an
// identity from a unit name: each caller passes the node and attempt key its own slot or grant carries,
// and the record read is checked against them before its launch manager is trusted.
fn session_launch_manager_reading_of(
  path: String,
  obs: FilesystemFileObservation,
  node_id: String,
  attempt_key: String,
) -> SessionLaunchManagerReading {
  match obs {
    FilesystemFileAbsent(_) => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: join(["the placement record ", path, " is not present"], "") }
    FilesystemFileRead { path: _, content } =>
      match parse_json_document(s: content) {
        JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap } => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: json_document_gap_text(gap: gap) }
        JsonDocumentParsed { value: doc } => {
          let decoded = session_placement_record_decode(doc: doc)
          match decoded.record {
            Absent => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: decoded.cause }
            Present { value: r } =>
              if r.node_id != node_id || r.attempt_key != attempt_key {
                LaunchManagerUnreadable {
                  detail: join(["the record at ", path, " belongs to ", r.node_id, " and ", r.attempt_key, ", not to ", node_id, " and ", attempt_key], ""),
                }
              } else {
                LaunchManagerRead { manager: r.launch_manager }
              }
          }
        }
      }
    FilesystemFileIndeterminate { cause } => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: cause }
    FilesystemFileObservationsDisagree { path: _, cause: c } => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: c }
    FilesystemFileSubjectRefused { directory: _, name: _, cause: c } => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: c }
  }
}

fn session_recorded_launch_manager(stores: SessionPlacementStores, node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> SessionLaunchManagerReading {
  let name = session_placement_record_basename(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)
  let path = join([stores.records_dir, "/", name], "")
  session_launch_manager_reading_of(
    path: path,
    obs: session_placement_file(dir: stores.records_dir, name: name),
    node_id: node_id,
    attempt_key: attempt_key,
  )
}

// THE SETTLEMENT'S ROUTE TO THE FACT. The pass hands its lifecycle reader a UNIT, and the only identity
// that unit carries without deriving it from its name is the one in its slot record -- which this pass
// reads anyway. So this reads that slot (one more read of the same file per settled unit, named rather
// than hidden) and takes the record's key from the identity the SLOT states.
fn session_recorded_launch_manager_for_unit(stores: SessionPlacementStores, unit: NonEmptyStr) -> SessionLaunchManagerReading {
  match attempt_slot_read(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: unit) {
    AttemptSlotHeld { record: rec, generation: _ } =>
      match session_attempt_name_of(identity: rec.identity) {
        Absent => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: join(["the slot for ", unit as String, " carries the identity ", rec.identity, ", which names no node and attempt key"], "") }
        Present { value: named } => session_recorded_launch_manager(stores: stores, node_id: named.node_id, attempt_key: named.attempt_key)
      }
    AttemptSlotAbsent => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: join(["the slot store holds no slot named ", unit as String, ", so no identity names a placement record to read"], "") }
    AttemptSlotUnreadable { detail: d } => LaunchManagerUnreadable { detail: d }
  }
}

// THE POOL THE SETTLEMENT FOLDS THE LEDGER UNDER, spelled once. The release route and the acquisition
// read must address the SAME pool, so both take it from here rather than each naming a number. The
// value is the one the release route has always used; what it should mean -- whether a release folds
// the history under the appropriation or under zero -- is a question this change does not touch, and
// changing it would move the very route the leaked leases come back through.
data session_ledger_fold_ceiling: Kibibyte = kibibyte(count: 0)

type SessionHolderEvidence {
  standing: UnitInvocationObservation
  boot: UnitBootObservation
  acquired_at: EpochSecs
}

type SessionHolderEvidenceReading
  = SessionHolderEvidenceRead { evidence: SessionHolderEvidence }
  | SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: String }

fn session_read_host_text(path: NonEmptyStr) -> FilesystemReadOutcome {
  let read = Filesystem.Read(path: path)
  filesystem_read_outcome(content: read.content, success: read.success, error: read.error)
}

// THE EVIDENCE A NOT-FOUND READING CAN BE BOUND TO, read from the places that hold it: the manager the
// LAUNCH RECORDED for this unit, the manager the reading was taken from, the host's current boot, and the
// ledger's acquisition instant for this lease reference. Every failure arm REFUSES with its reason; none
// answers with a default, because a default here manufactures death evidence -- an InvocationID that
// failed to read is not an absent one, and an acquisition instant that failed to read is not an old one.
// ADMISSIBILITY IS THE RECORDED FACT'S CALL: the reader no longer asks the unit's NAME whether it may
// read. It asks the placement record which manager ran the unit, compares that with the manager its
// reading comes from, and admits a pre-receipt lease only by the legacy list (session_launch_manager_admissible).
fn session_holder_evidence(stores: SessionPlacementStores, unit: NonEmptyStr, recorded: SessionLaunchManagerReading) -> SessionHolderEvidenceReading {
  let route = attempt_unit_route(unit: unit)
  match session_launch_manager_admissible(reading: recorded, route: route, reference: unit) {
    ManagerAdmissionRefused { detail } => SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: detail }
    // TWO ARMS, ONE BODY: this language has no or-pattern in a match arm, so the two admitted bases are
    // written out. A granted recorded fact and an admitted legacy lease reach the same reader; only the
    // REFUSED arm goes anywhere else, and it carries the reason the admission named.
    ManagerAdmissionGranted { manager: _ } => session_holder_evidence_from_manager(stores: stores, unit: unit, route: route)
    ManagerAdmissionLegacy { reference: _ } => session_holder_evidence_from_manager(stores: stores, unit: unit, route: route)
  }
}

// WHICH MANAGER THIS READER READS FROM, and what it therefore stamps. Its standing is the SYSTEM
// manager's, so a name claimed by a user-manager launcher is refused here rather than answered with the
// system manager's silence about a unit that lives elsewhere -- making a user-manager reading real needs
// the uid, which comes with the recorded-run follow-up. The Absent arm is unreachable through
// session_holder_evidence, which refuses an unclaimed name before calling this; it stays because this
// reader states its own limit instead of trusting its caller.
fn session_holder_evidence_from_manager(stores: SessionPlacementStores, unit: NonEmptyStr, route: UnitLaunchManagerRoute?) -> SessionHolderEvidenceReading {
  match route {
    Absent =>
      SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: join(["no launcher in the corpus claims a unit named ", unit as String, ", so no manager is declared for it; guessing one would manufacture a death reading taken from the wrong manager"], "") }
    Present { value: UnitRunOnUserManager } =>
      SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: join(["this reader takes and stamps the SYSTEM manager's standing, and ", unit as String, " is claimed by a user-manager launcher: the system manager's silence about a unit that lives on a user manager is not that unit's death"], "") }
    Present { value: UnitRunOnSystemManager } =>
      match compute_seat_acquisition_at(store: stores.store, partition: stores.partition, ceiling: session_ledger_fold_ceiling, reference: unit) {
        SeatAcquisitionNotHeld { reference: r } =>
          SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: join(["the ledger holds no acquisition for ", r as String, ": its acquisition instant cannot be read, and a missing instant is not an old one"], "") }
        SeatAcquisitionRefused { detail: d } => SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: d }
        SeatAcquisitionRead { reference: _, acquired_at: at, generation: _ } =>
          match attempt_unit_property(unit: unit, property: InvocationIDProperty) {
            AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason } => SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: join(["the unit's InvocationID standing could not be read: ", reason], "") }
            AttemptUnitAbsent => SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: "a property read does not answer whether a unit is absent, so the standing is not established" }
            AttemptUnitActive => SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: "a property read does not answer whether a unit is active, so the standing is not established" }
            AttemptUnitFinished { exit_status: invocation } =>
              match session_read_host_text(path: kernel_boot_id_path) {
                FilesystemReadRefused { error } => SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: join(["the host boot id could not be read: ", error], "") }
                FilesystemReadSucceeded { content: boot_text } =>
                  match session_read_host_text(path: proc_stat_path) {
                    FilesystemReadRefused { error } => SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: join(["the host boot instant could not be read: ", error], "") }
                    FilesystemReadSucceeded { content: stat_text } => SessionHolderEvidenceRead { evidence: SessionHolderEvidence {
                      standing: unit_invocation_observation(manager: SystemManager, unit: unit, boot_id_text: boot_text, proc_stat_text: stat_text, invocation_text: invocation),
                      boot: unit_boot_observation(boot_id_text: boot_text, proc_stat_text: stat_text),
                      acquired_at: at,
                    } }
                  }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

// WHAT A UNIT THE MANAGER NO LONGER HAS PROVES, once the reading is bound to the holder's identity.
// The exit artifact enters only as a NOTE on the answer: an artifact is a fact about its writer, and it
// never decides this. The proof itself is the conjunction in gunbc.systemd_unit_invocation_liveness
// unit_reboot_holder_liveness -- no unit in the manager that ran it, AND a boot that began after the
// ledger acquired this hold.
fn session_absent_unit_lifecycle(evidence: SessionHolderEvidenceReading, holder_unit: NonEmptyStr, artifact_note: String) -> UnitLifecycle {
  match evidence {
    SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail } => UnitLifecycleUnknown { detail: join(["the unit is not in the manager, and its holder identity is not established: ", detail], "") }
    SessionHolderEvidenceRead { evidence: e } =>
      // The manager named for this holder is the system manager, and it is named that way honestly:
      // session_holder_evidence admits only a unit whose RECORDED launch manager is the system manager
      // (or a lease listed as predating the receipt) AND whose reading this reader takes from the system
      // manager, and it stamps the standing with that same manager. The liveness arm re-checks the
      // binding, so a standing read from another manager, or about another unit, cannot free this seat.
      match unit_reboot_holder_liveness(standing: e.standing, holder_unit: holder_unit, holder_manager: SystemManager, boot: e.boot, acquired_at: e.acquired_at, skew_bound_seconds: session_holder_boot_skew_bound_seconds) {
        HolderObservedDead { evidence: proof } => UnitTerminatedCauseUnknown { detail: join([proof, artifact_note], "") }
        HolderObservedLive { evidence: proof } => UnitStillRunning { detail: join([proof, artifact_note], "") }
        HolderLivenessUnobservable { cause } => UnitLifecycleUnknown { detail: join(["the holder's death is not observable: ", cause, artifact_note], "") }
      }
  }
}

fn session_unit_lifecycle(o: AttemptUnitObservation) -> UnitLifecycle {
  match o {
    // A BARE NOT-FOUND IS NOT A VERDICT. A transient unit is collected when its process ends, so the
    // manager not having it is equally the state of a unit whose manager restarted. What may free a seat
    // is session_absent_unit_lifecycle, which binds the reading to the holder's identity; this reader
    // carries no such binding, so it refuses rather than inferring.
    AttemptUnitAbsent => UnitLifecycleUnknown { detail: "the manager has no unit by this name; that standing is bound to the holder's identity by session_absent_unit_lifecycle, never here" }
    AttemptUnitActive => UnitStillRunning { detail: "the unit is active" }
    AttemptUnitFinished { exit_status } =>
      if exit_status == "0" { UnitTerminatedSuccess { detail: "ExecMainStatus=0" } } else { UnitTerminatedFailure { detail: join(["ExecMainStatus=", exit_status], "") } }
    AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason } => UnitLifecycleUnknown { detail: reason }
  }
}

// THE ABANDONMENT ROUTE'S READ. It consults no exit spool of its own, but the seat it frees is the same
// seat, so a not-found unit is bound to the holder's identity here exactly as the settlement binds it.
fn session_observe_unit_lifecycle(stores: SessionPlacementStores, unit: NonEmptyStr, recorded: SessionLaunchManagerReading) -> UnitLifecycle {
  let observed = attempt_unit_observation(unit: unit)
  match observed {
    AttemptUnitAbsent => session_absent_unit_lifecycle(
      evidence: session_holder_evidence(stores: stores, unit: unit, recorded: recorded),
      holder_unit: unit,
      artifact_note: " (read on the abandonment route, which consults no exit spool)",
    )
    AttemptUnitActive => session_unit_lifecycle(o: observed)
    AttemptUnitFinished { exit_status: _ } => session_unit_lifecycle(o: observed)
    AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason: _ } => session_unit_lifecycle(o: observed)
  }
}

// THE SETTLEMENT'S READ OF A WORKER UNIT, now that the unit is collected when its process ends
// (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator dispatch_worker_unit_properties). A loaded unit is read as before;
// a collected one is read from its exit record, so a worker that exited 0 settles as SUCCESS rather
// than as cause-unknown. A collected unit with NO record, or with only a defective record, is read
// through the holder's identity: the seat is freed only when the manager that ran the unit has no such
// unit AND the host's boot began after the ledger acquired this hold (session_absent_unit_lifecycle).
// The settlement asks whether the holder is gone, not whether the evidence is old, and still frees only
// after the launch deadline (session_settle_decide). The settlement asks whether the unit's lifetime is
// over, not whether a worker ran, so it needs no start receipt: the slot it is settling IS one.
fn session_worker_unit_lifecycle(unit: NonEmptyStr, loaded: AttemptUnitObservation, record: AttemptExitRecordObservation, evidence: SessionHolderEvidenceReading) -> UnitLifecycle {
  match loaded {
    AttemptUnitAbsent =>
      match record {
        // NO ARTIFACT AT ALL: the only evidence is the unit's standing, bound to the holder's identity.
        AttemptExitRecordNone =>
          session_absent_unit_lifecycle(evidence: evidence, holder_unit: unit, artifact_note: " (the spool holds no exit record for this unit)")
        AttemptExitRecordFound { record: _ } => session_unit_lifecycle(o: attempt_unit_from_exit_record(unit: unit, record: record, start: AttemptUnitStartRecorded))
        // THE ARTIFACT IS ABOUT ITS WRITER, NOT ABOUT THE HOLDER. An entry whose name still spells the
        // stop variables was created without the manager's substitution: the hook's writer is broken, and
        // that says nothing about whether the process ended. So this arm neither keeps the seat on the
        // artifact's authority nor frees it on the artifact's authority: it names the defect -- variables
        // and entries, so it is countable -- and hands the decision to the unit's standing in the manager
        // that ran it, exactly as if the spool held nothing. A malformed artifact is never death proof, and
        // naming it is not licence to release; it enters only as a note on the answer the holder's identity
        // gives (the arms in gunbc.systemd_unit_invocation_liveness).
        AttemptExitRecordWriterUnsubstituted { entries, variables } =>
          session_absent_unit_lifecycle(
            evidence: evidence,
            holder_unit: unit,
            artifact_note: join([" (its only exit artifact names the stop variables unexpanded (", join(variables, ", "), "): a defective writer, which is not evidence either way: ", join(entries, ", ")], ""),
          )
        AttemptExitRecordUnreadable { reason } => UnitLifecycleUnknown { detail: reason }
      }
    AttemptUnitActive => session_unit_lifecycle(o: loaded)
    AttemptUnitFinished { exit_status: _ } => session_unit_lifecycle(o: loaded)
    AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason: _ } => session_unit_lifecycle(o: loaded)
  }
}

// THE SAME READ WITH THE MANAGER'S STANDING AND THE HOLDER'S EVIDENCE SUPPLIED. Production reaches it
// through session_worker_unit_lifecycle_for_instance, which passes attempt_unit_observation's real read
// and session_holder_evidence's real readings; a witness seeds them, because a unit and the host's boot
// are facts of the manager and the kernel and no file a witness writes can be one. Everything else --
// the spool listing, the matching, the settlement -- stays the production path over the real fixture
// root. One authority, one matcher, one seeded seam.
fn session_worker_unit_lifecycle_with_standing(instance: HostDashboardInstance, unit: NonEmptyStr, loaded: AttemptUnitObservation, evidence: SessionHolderEvidenceReading) -> UnitLifecycle {
  match loaded {
    AttemptUnitAbsent =>
      session_worker_unit_lifecycle(
        unit: unit,
        loaded: loaded,
        evidence: evidence,
        record: attempt_exit_record_matching(
          matches: s => match s {
            RoadmapEntrySubject { node_id: n, attempt_key: a, role: r, invocation_id: _ } =>
              r == attempt_unit_role_token(role: AttemptWorkerRole) && (match dispatch_attempt_unit_name(node_id: n, attempt_key: a) {
                SystemdUnitNameAdmitted { name } => (systemd_unit_name_wire(name: name) as String) == (unit as String)
                SystemdUnitNameStemEmpty => false
                SystemdUnitNameDisallowedCharacter { stem: _, character: _ } => false
                SystemdUnitNameOverlong { length: _ } => false
              })
            // A COMPUTE SEAT'S RECORD IS NOT THIS ATTEMPT'S WORKER, and an entry too broken to say which
            // route wrote it cannot be attributed to this unit. Both answer "not mine", so neither can
            // make a seat's exit stand in for a worker's -- the confusion this split exists to make
            // unrepresentable.
            ComputeEntrySubject { identity: _, invocation_id: _ } => false
            OtherEntrySubject { parts: _ } => false
          },
          listings: attempt_exit_stage_listings(instance_root: instance.instance_root as String),
        ),
      )
    AttemptUnitActive => session_unit_lifecycle(o: loaded)
    AttemptUnitFinished { exit_status: _ } => session_unit_lifecycle(o: loaded)
    AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason: _ } => session_unit_lifecycle(o: loaded)
  }
}

fn session_worker_unit_lifecycle_for_instance(instance: HostDashboardInstance, unit: NonEmptyStr) -> UnitLifecycle {
  match session_placement_stores(instance: instance) {
    SessionStoresUnresolved { detail } =>
      session_worker_unit_lifecycle_with_standing(
        instance: instance,
        unit: unit,
        loaded: attempt_unit_observation(unit: unit),
        evidence: SessionHolderEvidenceRefused { detail: join(["the session ledger is not resolvable, so the instant this hold was acquired cannot be read: ", detail], "") },
      )
    // THE SETTLEMENT READER GETS THE FACT FROM THE RECORD, not from the unit's name: the pass hands it a
    // unit, the slot for that unit states the identity, and the record filed under that identity says
    // which manager ran the unit. Where any link is missing the reading is LaunchManagerUnreadable, and
    // the holder route refuses with that reason -- the seat keeps its charge.
    SessionStoresResolved { stores } =>
      session_worker_unit_lifecycle_with_standing(
        instance: instance,
        unit: unit,
        loaded: attempt_unit_observation(unit: unit),
        evidence: session_holder_evidence(
          stores: stores,
          unit: unit,
          recorded: session_recorded_launch_manager_for_unit(stores: stores, unit: unit),
        ),
      )
  }
}

// THE START RECEIPT THE PROCESS OBSERVER NEEDS (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator
// AttemptUnitStartStanding): this attempt's placement record. It is written immediately before the
// worker unit is started, so its presence means dispatch committed to a unit; its absence means the
// attempt never had one.
fn session_worker_start_standing(observation: SessionPlacementObservation) -> AttemptUnitStartStanding {
  match observation {
    SessionPlacementObserved { slot: _, grant: _, returned: _ } => AttemptUnitStartRecorded
    SessionPlacementAbsent { unit: _ } => AttemptUnitNeverStarted
    SessionPlacementUnreadable { unit: _, detail } => AttemptUnitStartUnread { reason: detail }
    SessionPlacementForeign { unit: _, detail } => AttemptUnitStartUnread { reason: detail }
    SessionPlacementUnnameable { detail } => AttemptUnitStartUnread { reason: detail }
  }
}

// THE WORKER'S PROCESS OBSERVATION FOR ONE ATTEMPT: the unit, else its exit record, else -- only when
// both are silent -- whether it was ever started. Each later read is taken only when the earlier one
// could not answer, so a running worker costs one manager read as before.
fn attempt_worker_unit_observe_for_instance(instance: HostDashboardInstance, node_id: String, attempt_key: String) -> AttemptUnitObservation {
  match dispatch_attempt_unit_name(node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key) {
    SystemdUnitNameStemEmpty =>
      AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason: systemd_unit_name_refusal_detail(admission: SystemdUnitNameStemEmpty) }
    SystemdUnitNameDisallowedCharacter { stem: s, character: ch } =>
      AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason: systemd_unit_name_refusal_detail(admission: SystemdUnitNameDisallowedCharacter { stem: s, character: ch }) }
    SystemdUnitNameOverlong { length: n } =>
      AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason: systemd_unit_name_refusal_detail(admission: SystemdUnitNameOverlong { length: n }) }
    SystemdUnitNameAdmitted { name } => {
  let unit = systemd_unit_name_wire(name: name)
  let loaded = attempt_unit_observation(unit: unit)
  match loaded {
    AttemptUnitAbsent => {
      let record = attempt_exit_record_observe(instance_root: instance.instance_root as String, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key, role: AttemptWorkerRole)
      match record {
        AttemptExitRecordNone =>
          attempt_worker_unit_observation_of(unit: unit, loaded: loaded, record: record, start: session_worker_start_standing(observation: session_placement_observe_for_attempt(instance: instance, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)))
        AttemptExitRecordFound { record: _ } => attempt_worker_unit_observation_of(unit: unit, loaded: loaded, record: record, start: AttemptUnitStartRecorded)
        AttemptExitRecordUnreadable { reason: _ } => attempt_worker_unit_observation_of(unit: unit, loaded: loaded, record: record, start: AttemptUnitStartRecorded)
        // Not even proof of the start: an entry that still spells the stop variables was written by
        // something that never substituted them, and it is not known to be this unit's hook. The start
        // standing is READ, as in the no-record arm. The observation stays indeterminate either way.
        AttemptExitRecordWriterUnsubstituted { entries: _, variables: _ } => attempt_worker_unit_observation_of(unit: unit, loaded: loaded, record: record, start: session_worker_start_standing(observation: session_placement_observe_for_attempt(instance: instance, node_id: node_id, attempt_key: attempt_key)))
      }
    }
    AttemptUnitActive => loaded
    AttemptUnitFinished { exit_status: _ } => loaded
    AttemptUnitUnreadable { reason: _ } => loaded
  }
    }
  }
}

// THE DECISION, PURE OVER ONE SLOT. Every arm that does not release says why, and every arm that
// releases names the generation it will close.
type SessionSettleDecision
  = SettleTerminateAndRelease { record: AttemptRecord, generation: CasGeneration, attempt: SessionAttemptName, reason: String }
  // A SLOT WHOSE CHARGE WAS ALREADY RETURNED IS CLOSED AS BOOKKEEPING, NOT RELEASED (operator ruling
  // 2026-11-04, after the srv1 Oct-14 lease was released in the ledger while its slot sat under a root no
  // pass enumerated). The ordinary close needs the holder's death, and the death is dated from the
  // acquisition instant, which the folded pool stops carrying once the charge is back -- so a slot that
  // becomes reachable afterwards can never satisfy recovery_trigger and would sit launching forever,
  // listed to the serve as an attempt with no seat.
  //
  // THE CONDITION IS POSITIVE, NOT THE ABSENCE OF A HOLD. This arm fires only when the partition's own
  // history shows the acquisition AND a return after it (gunbc.compute.host_capacity
  // .compute_seat_charge_returned). Mere "the pool holds no term" is not enough: it is also the state of a
  // slot whose acquisition has not been written yet, and retiring that would destroy the only record of an
  // attempt that may be about to run. If the history cannot show the return, the slot is kept, with the
  // charge reading named in the reason.
  //
  // IT NEVER CALLS compute_release_on. Nothing is being freed; the ledger already returned this charge. The
  // detail says so and makes no holder-death claim -- the transition's whole content is "the record and the
  // ledger no longer agree, and the ledger is right".
  | SettleRetireUncharged { record: AttemptRecord, generation: CasGeneration, attempt: SessionAttemptName, returned_at: EpochSecs, by: ChargeReturnCause, ledger_generation: Nat, trigger_reading: String }
  | SettleReleaseOnly { record: AttemptRecord, attempt: SessionAttemptName, reason: String }
  | SettleKeep { why: String, explain: Bool }
  | SettleDone { why: String }

// THE ONE ADMISSION OF A SLOT TO SETTLEMENT. Whether a held slot may be closed and its seat released under
// THIS name is a single fact, and both deciders below (the pass's session_settle_decide and the operator's
// session_operator_settle_decide) consume it, so neither can admit what the other refuses. A slot is
// admitted only when its identity names a node and attempt, the key it is read under IS the reference it
// records, and its reference, unit and identity all name that one attempt (session_slot_binding_mismatch).
type SlotSettlementAdmission
  = SlotAdmissionAbsent
  | SlotAdmissionUnreadable { detail: String }
  | SlotAdmissionUnbindable { identity: String }
  | SlotAdmissionForeign { mismatch: String }
  | SlotAdmissionAdmitted { record: AttemptRecord, generation: CasGeneration, attempt: SessionAttemptName }

fn session_slot_settlement_admission(key: NonEmptyStr, slot: AttemptSlotReading) -> SlotSettlementAdmission {
  match slot {
    AttemptSlotAbsent => SlotAdmissionAbsent
    AttemptSlotUnreadable { detail } => SlotAdmissionUnreadable { detail: detail }
    AttemptSlotHeld { record: rec, generation: g } =>
      match session_attempt_name_of(identity: rec.identity) {
        Absent => SlotAdmissionUnbindable { identity: rec.identity }
        Present { value: name } => {
          let mismatch = if (key as String) != rec.reference { join(["the slot keyed ", key as String, " names reference ", rec.reference], "") } else { session_slot_binding_mismatch(record: rec, node_id: name.node_id, attempt_key: name.attempt_key) }
          if mismatch != "" { SlotAdmissionForeign { mismatch: mismatch } } else { SlotAdmissionAdmitted { record: rec, generation: g, attempt: name } }
        }
      }
  }
}

// THE SEAT-KEEPING WORDS FOR A SLOT THAT IS NOT ADMITTED, spelled once for both deciders.
fn session_slot_unreadable_keep(key: NonEmptyStr, detail: String) -> SessionSettleDecision {
  SettleKeep { why: join(["the session slot for ", key as String, " is unreadable, and an unreadable slot is not an absent one, so its seat is kept: ", detail], ""), explain: true }
}

fn session_slot_unbindable_keep(key: NonEmptyStr, identity: String) -> SessionSettleDecision {
  SettleKeep { why: join(["the session slot ", key as String, " binds identity ", identity, ", which names no node and attempt, so its seat is kept"], ""), explain: true }
}

fn session_slot_foreign_keep(key: NonEmptyStr, mismatch: String) -> SessionSettleDecision {
  SettleKeep { why: join(["the session slot ", key as String, " is not bound consistently (", mismatch, "), so it is never released under this name"], ""), explain: true }
}

fn session_settle_decide(key: NonEmptyStr, slot: AttemptSlotReading, lifecycle: UnitLifecycle, now: EpochSecs, release_settled: Bool, charge: ComputeSeatCharge) -> SessionSettleDecision {
  match session_slot_settlement_admission(key: key, slot: slot) {
    SlotAdmissionAbsent => SettleDone { why: join(["no slot is held for ", key as String], "") }
    SlotAdmissionUnreadable { detail } => session_slot_unreadable_keep(key: key, detail: detail)
    SlotAdmissionUnbindable { identity } => session_slot_unbindable_keep(key: key, identity: identity)
    SlotAdmissionForeign { mismatch } => session_slot_foreign_keep(key: key, mismatch: mismatch)
    SlotAdmissionAdmitted { record: rec, generation: g, attempt: name } =>
      match rec.state {
        AttemptTerminal { verdict: _, detail: d } =>
          if release_settled {
            SettleDone { why: "closed and released" }
          } else {
            // A CLOSED SLOT WITH NO SETTLED-RELEASE RECORD HAS TWO CAUSES, AND THE LEDGER'S OWN HISTORY TELLS
            // THEM APART. The arm that was here before assumed the second one: the seat is still out and the
            // pass owes a release. But a slot can be closed while its charge is already back -- that is the
            // state a real lease was put into on 2026-11-04, when a release ran by reference while the slot sat
            // under a root no pass enumerates. The partition's own history then shows acquire-then-return, and a
            // release issued here would return a charge the ledger already closed (and for such a reference the
            // acquisition instant is gone, so compute_release_on could not even be fenced on it). The pass
            // answers Done and SAYS the release record is missing, which is the honest residue; it never calls
            // compute_release_on a second time. When the history does NOT positively show the return, the old
            // arm stands unchanged.
            match charge {
              SeatChargeReturned { returned_at: back, by: cause, reference: _ } =>
                SettleDone { why: join(["closed, and its charge is already back in the ledger (returned at ", to_string(value: back), ", ", charge_return_cause_wire(c: cause), ") while the settled-release record for this slot is missing; there is nothing left to settle and no second release is issued"], "") }
              other => SettleReleaseOnly { record: rec, attempt: name, reason: join(["the slot is closed (", d, ") and no settled release is recorded"], "") }
            }
          }
        // A RESERVED slot is inside its producer's own declared window; the producer is expected to act on it,
        // and a charge returned under a reserved slot is a different defect whose remedy is not to retire the
        // record. Left exactly as it was, on purpose.
        AttemptReserved => session_settle_by_trigger(record: rec, generation: g, attempt: name, trigger: recovery_trigger(record: rec, lifecycle: lifecycle, now: now))
        // A LAUNCHING SLOT IS DECIDED BY TWO INDEPENDENT READINGS, AND THE LEDGER'S OWN HISTORY IS ASKED FIRST:
        // whether this reference's charge is already back in the capacity partition (compute_seat_charge_returned,
        // reading that partition's own history), and whether the holder can be observed (lifecycle, and through
        // it the recovery trigger).
        //   A charge that is ALREADY BACK, under a holder that is not observed alive, means the lease is home.
        //     The slot is retired as bookkeeping and NO release is issued: a second compute_release_on would set
        //     up a second authority over one appropriation, and for these references the acquisition instant is
        //     no longer in the ledger at all, so a release could not even be fenced on it. That is the shape the
        //     2026-10-28 lease was left in, and the state the release by hand on 2026-11-04 produced for the
        //     2026-10-14 one.
        //   UnitStillRunning is exempt, always. A charge returned under a holder the manager reports running is
        //     a different defect -- the release was issued while the holder lived -- and closing that slot would
        //     burn the only handle on the seat. The keep names that instead.
        //   Charge held, never acquired, or unproven: the ordinary trigger, unchanged, with the charge reading
        //     appended to whatever keep it returns.
        AttemptLaunching => session_launching_settlement(rec: rec, generation: g, attempt: name, lifecycle: lifecycle, now: now, charge: charge)
      }
  }
}

// THE LAUNCHING ARM, factored out of the match so the recovery trigger is computed ONCE and shared by every
// branch that consults it (gunbc.design_argument::minimize_redundancy: share the first value). It is not a cosmetic binding: the trigger reading
// is what a retirement records as the thing its decision rested on, and the ordinary settle route consumes the
// same value. Two calls would be two readings of one decision, and the first review of this code found exactly
// that shape here.
fn session_launching_settlement(rec: AttemptRecord, generation: CasGeneration, attempt: SessionAttemptName, lifecycle: UnitLifecycle, now: EpochSecs, charge: ComputeSeatCharge) -> SessionSettleDecision {
  let trigger = recovery_trigger(record: rec, lifecycle: lifecycle, now: now)
  match lifecycle {
    UnitStillRunning { detail: live } =>
      SettleKeep { why: join(["the unit still reports itself running (", live, "), so the recovery trigger does not fire; and because the holder is OBSERVED ALIVE, a charge the ledger already returned is a different defect: the release was issued while the holder lived, and closing this slot would drop the only handle on its seat"], ""), explain: true }
    _ =>
      match charge {
        SeatChargeReturned { returned_at: back, by: cause, generation: lg, acquired_at: _, reference: _ } =>
          SettleRetireUncharged { record: rec, generation: generation, attempt: attempt, returned_at: back, by: cause, ledger_generation: lg, trigger_reading: recovery_trigger_wire(t: trigger) }
        other =>
          match session_settle_by_trigger(record: rec, generation: generation, attempt: attempt, trigger: trigger) {
            SettleKeep { why: keep, explain: explain } => SettleKeep { why: join([keep, "; and the ledger does not positively show this charge as returned: ", compute_seat_charge_wire(c: other)], ""), explain: explain }
            settled => settled
          }
      }
  }
}

// THE OPERATOR-DIRECTED DECISION, over the same admission. The operator supplies the evidence that the
// holder is gone (the reason carries what it read); the pass observes nothing here, so the record says the
// operator directed the closure and never that the pass saw the holder end. Absent from the CURRENT store
// refuses: releasing the ledger while the slot sits where no pass reads it would erase the acquisition
// instant session_holder_evidence needs (it reads it from the ledger), so such a slot is first carried into
// the current store. Everything the admission refuses keeps its seat, with the pass's own words.
fn session_operator_settle_decide(key: NonEmptyStr, slot: AttemptSlotReading, reason: NonEmptyStr, release_settled: Bool) -> SessionSettleDecision {
  let directed = join(["operator-directed: ", reason as String], "")
  match session_slot_settlement_admission(key: key, slot: slot) {
    SlotAdmissionAbsent => SettleKeep { why: join(["no slot for ", key as String, " is in the current store, so nothing is released: a ledger-only release would erase the acquisition instant the settle pass needs to prove the holder died; carry the slot into the current store first"], ""), explain: false }
    SlotAdmissionUnreadable { detail } => session_slot_unreadable_keep(key: key, detail: detail)
    SlotAdmissionUnbindable { identity } => session_slot_unbindable_keep(key: key, identity: identity)
    SlotAdmissionForeign { mismatch } => session_slot_foreign_keep(key: key, mismatch: mismatch)
    SlotAdmissionAdmitted { record: rec, generation: g, attempt: name } =>
      match rec.state {
        AttemptTerminal { verdict: _, detail: d } =>
          if release_settled { SettleDone { why: "closed and released" } } else { SettleReleaseOnly { record: rec, attempt: name, reason: join([directed, "; the slot is closed (", d, ") and no settled release is recorded"], "") } }
        AttemptReserved => SettleTerminateAndRelease { record: rec, generation: g, attempt: name, reason: directed }
        AttemptLaunching => SettleTerminateAndRelease { record: rec, generation: g, attempt: name, reason: directed }
      }
  }
}

fn session_settle_by_trigger(record: AttemptRecord, generation: CasGeneration, attempt: SessionAttemptName, trigger: RecoveryTrigger) -> SessionSettleDecision {
  match trigger {
    RecoveryMayTerminate { reason } => SettleTerminateAndRelease { record: record, generation: generation, attempt: attempt, reason: reason }
    RecoveryTooEarly { deadline: d, now: n } => SettleKeep { why: recovery_trigger_wire(t: RecoveryTooEarly { deadline: d, now: n }), explain: false }
    RecoveryUnitNotEnded { lifecycle: u } => SettleKeep { why: recovery_trigger_wire(t: RecoveryUnitNotEnded { lifecycle: u }), explain: false }
    RecoveryTerminalRecordMayRelease { state: s } => SettleDone { why: recovery_trigger_wire(t: RecoveryTerminalRecordMayRelease { state: s }) }
  }
}

type SessionSettlement
  = SessionSettlementReleaseAttempted { unit: String, freed: ComputeRelease, detail: String }
  | SessionSettlementKept { unit: String, why: String }
  | SessionSettlementDone { unit: String, why: String }
  | SessionSettlementRefused { unit: String, detail: String }
  // The slot was closed and NOTHING was released, because the charge was already back. Distinct from
  // ReleaseAttempted on purpose: a count of releases that included this row would report capacity returned
  // twice (the operator ruling 2026-11-04).
  | SessionSettlementRetiredUncharged { unit: String, attempt: SessionAttemptName, detail: String }

type SessionSettlePass
  = SessionSettlePassRan { settlements: List<SessionSettlement> }
  | SessionSettlePassRefused { detail: String }

fn session_settlement_wire(s: SessionSettlement) -> String {
  match s {
    SessionSettlementReleaseAttempted { unit, freed, detail } => join([unit, ": ", session_release_outcome_wire(r: freed), " (", detail, ")"], "")
    SessionSettlementKept { unit, why } => join([unit, ": kept (", why, ")"], "")
    SessionSettlementDone { unit, why } => join([unit, ": done (", why, ")"], "")
    SessionSettlementRefused { unit, detail } => join([unit, ": REFUSED (", detail, ")"], "")
    SessionSettlementRetiredUncharged { unit, detail } => join([unit, ": retired uncharged (", detail, ")"], "")
  }
}

fn session_settle_pass_wire(p: SessionSettlePass) -> String {
  match p {
    SessionSettlePassRan { settlements } => join(map(settlements, s => session_settlement_wire(s: s)), "; ")
    SessionSettlePassRefused { detail } => join(["session settlement refused: ", detail], "")
  }
}

// THE KEPT-BUT-UNRESOLVABLE CASES LEAVE A DURABLE EXPLANATION. A slot that cannot be read, or that is
// bound inconsistently, keeps its seat -- the safe direction -- and an operator learns why from a note
// beside the records, rewritten each pass, instead of from an unexplained shortfall in the pool.
fn session_settle_note(stores: SessionPlacementStores, unit: String, why: String) -> String {
  let path = join([stores.records_dir, "/", session_placement_note_basename(unit: unit)], "")
  let w = Filesystem.Write(path: path, content: why)
  if w.success { why } else { join([why, " (note not written at ", path, ": ", w.error, ")"], "") }
}

fn session_release_settled_for_slot(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, slot: AttemptSlotReading) -> Bool {
  match slot {
    AttemptSlotHeld { record: rec, generation: _ } =>
      match session_attempt_name_of(identity: rec.identity) {
        Absent => false
        Present { value: n } =>
          match session_placement_observe_at(stores: stores, host: host, node_id: n.node_id, attempt_key: n.attempt_key) {
            SessionPlacementObserved { slot: _, grant: _, returned } => session_release_settled(r: returned)
            SessionPlacementAbsent { unit: _ } => false
            SessionPlacementUnreadable { unit: _, detail: _ } => false
            SessionPlacementForeign { unit: _, detail: _ } => false
            SessionPlacementUnnameable { detail: _ } => false
          }
      }
    AttemptSlotAbsent => false
    AttemptSlotUnreadable { detail: _ } => false
  }
}

// THE ONE EXECUTION OF A SETTLE DECISION, for the pass and for the operator. A terminate runs at the
// generation the decision read (a CAS): a slot that moved refuses and releases nothing. `closing` renders the
// terminal slot's detail from the decision's reason; it is the only thing the two callers say differently.
fn session_settle_execute(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, key: NonEmptyStr, decision: SessionSettleDecision, closing: fn(String) -> String) -> SessionSettlement {
  match decision {
    SettleDone { why } => SessionSettlementDone { unit: key as String, why: why }
    SettleKeep { why, explain } =>
      SessionSettlementKept { unit: key as String, why: if explain { session_settle_note(stores: stores, unit: key as String, why: why) } else { why } }
    SettleReleaseOnly { record: _, attempt, reason } =>
      session_settle_release(stores: stores, host: host, unit: key, attempt: attempt, reason: reason)
    SettleTerminateAndRelease { record, generation, attempt, reason } =>
      match attempt_terminate(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: record.reference as NonEmptyStr, expected: generation, verdict: AttemptRecovered, detail: closing(reason)) {
        AttemptLostRace { expected: e, observed: o } =>
          SessionSettlementRefused { unit: key as String, detail: join(["the slot moved while settlement was deciding (expected ", e, ", found ", o, "); the observation is stale, so nothing is released"], "") }
        AttemptTransitionRefused { detail: d } => SessionSettlementRefused { unit: key as String, detail: join(["the slot would not take the terminal generation: ", d], "") }
        AttemptAdvanced { state: _, generation: _ } => session_settle_release(stores: stores, host: host, unit: key, attempt: attempt, reason: reason)
      }
    SettleRetireUncharged { record, generation, attempt: name, returned_at, by: cause, ledger_generation, trigger_reading } =>
      match attempt_terminate(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: record.reference as NonEmptyStr, expected: generation, verdict: AttemptRecovered, detail: join(["charge returned at ledger generation ", to_string(value: ledger_generation), " at ", to_string(value: returned_at), " (", charge_return_cause_wire(c: cause), "); the slot is retired as bookkeeping: no release is issued and no holder-death claim is made. What would otherwise have kept it: ", trigger_reading], "")) {
        AttemptLostRace { expected: e, observed: o } =>
          SessionSettlementRefused { unit: key as String, detail: join(["the slot moved while settlement was deciding (expected ", e, ", found ", o, "); the observation is stale, so nothing is retired"], "") }
        AttemptTransitionRefused { detail: d } => SessionSettlementRefused { unit: key as String, detail: join(["the slot would not take the terminal generation: ", d], "") }
        AttemptAdvanced { state: st, generation: g } =>
          SessionSettlementRetiredUncharged {
            unit: key as String,
            attempt: name,
            detail: join(["slot closed at generation ", to_string(value: cas_generation_count(g: g)), " (state ", attempt_state_wire(s: st), "); charge was already returned at ledger generation ", to_string(value: ledger_generation), ", so no release was issued"], ""),
          }
      }
  }
}

fn session_settle_one(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, key: NonEmptyStr, lifecycle: UnitLifecycle, now: EpochSecs, charge: ComputeSeatCharge) -> SessionSettlement {
  // The charge for this key arrives from the pass, which reads the capacity partition ONCE for all the keys
  // (session_settle_keys). One key's settle therefore costs one slot read, one lifecycle observation and one
  // map lookup -- not another walk of the event chain.
  let slot = attempt_slot_read(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: key)
  session_settle_execute(
    stores: stores, host: host, key: key,
    decision: session_settle_decide(key: key, slot: slot, lifecycle: lifecycle, now: now, release_settled: session_release_settled_for_slot(stores: stores, host: host, slot: slot), charge: charge),
    closing: r => join([r, "; unit ", unit_lifecycle_wire(u: lifecycle)], ""),
  )
}

// THE OPERATOR'S SETTLEMENT OF ONE NAMED SLOT: the same read, admission and execution as the pass, with the
// operator's decision in place of the pass's observation of the unit.
fn session_operator_settle_one(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, key: NonEmptyStr, reason: NonEmptyStr) -> SessionSettlement {
  let slot = attempt_slot_read(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: key)
  session_settle_execute(
    stores: stores, host: host, key: key,
    decision: session_operator_settle_decide(key: key, slot: slot, reason: reason, release_settled: session_release_settled_for_slot(stores: stores, host: host, slot: slot)),
    closing: r => r,
  )
}

// THE RELEASE SETTLEMENT PERFORMS, bound to the grant the placement record names when there is one.
// A slot whose placement record was never written releases by its reference with no grant binding;
// the ledger answers NothingToRelease if the reservation never landed.
fn session_settle_release(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, unit: NonEmptyStr, attempt: SessionAttemptName, reason: String) -> SessionSettlement {
  let binding = match session_placement_observe_at(stores: stores, host: host, node_id: attempt.node_id, attempt_key: attempt.attempt_key) {
    SessionPlacementObserved { slot: _, grant, returned: _ } =>
      match grant {
        SessionGrantRecorded { record } => Present { value: SessionGrantBinding { grant_identity: record.grant_identity, fence_generation: record.fence_generation } }
        SessionGrantNotRecorded { path: _ } => none
        SessionGrantUnreadable { path: _, detail: _ } => none
        SessionGrantForeign { path: _, detail: _ } => none
      }
    SessionPlacementAbsent { unit: _ } => none
    SessionPlacementUnreadable { unit: _, detail: _ } => none
    SessionPlacementForeign { unit: _, detail: _ } => none
    SessionPlacementUnnameable { detail: _ } => none
  }
  let why = join(["settled: ", reason], "") as NonEmptyStr
  let freed = compute_release_on(store: stores.store, partition: stores.partition, appropriation: session_ledger_fold_ceiling, reference: unit, reason: why)
  let write = session_placement_release_write(records_dir: stores.records_dir, node_id: attempt.node_id, attempt_key: attempt.attempt_key, grant_binding: binding, reason: why, freed: freed)
  SessionSettlementReleaseAttempted { unit: unit as String, freed: freed, detail: join([reason, session_write_note(w: write)], "") }
}

// THE SLOT RECORDS A CLIENT FOLLOWS AFTER A 202. A dispatch whose attempt-unit start request was
// enqueued but not yet answered (SpawnLaunchPending) leaves its placement slot "launching"; the
// served /attempts.json carries every slot through attempt_record_json (the one serializer), each
// naming its owner_node and state, so the client reads that node's slot until it is no longer
// launching. A slot that cannot be read is carried as its own refusal, never dropped.
type SessionSlotRecords
  = SessionSlotRecordsRead { records: List<AttemptRecord>, unreadable: List<String> }
  | SessionSlotRecordsRefused { detail: String }

// ONE READ PER SLOT: each key is read once into this classification, then records and unreadable are
// projections of the same reads, so a slot that changes state mid-serve cannot appear in both lists or
// neither, and the lists are built by flat_map rather than a copied accumulator.
type SessionSlotObserved
  = SessionSlotObservedHeld { record: AttemptRecord }
  | SessionSlotObservedUnreadable { line: String }
  | SessionSlotObservedAbsent

fn session_placement_slot_records(stores: SessionPlacementStores) -> SessionSlotRecords {
  match attempt_slot_keys(store: stores.slots.slots) {
    AttemptSlotKeysListed { keys } => {
      let observed = map(keys, k => match attempt_slot_read(store: stores.slots.slots, reference: k) {
        AttemptSlotHeld { record: r, generation: _ } => SessionSlotObservedHeld { record: r }
        AttemptSlotAbsent => SessionSlotObservedAbsent
        AttemptSlotUnreadable { detail: d } => SessionSlotObservedUnreadable { line: join([k as String, ": ", d], "") }
      })
      SessionSlotRecordsRead {
        records: flat_map(observed, o => match o {
          SessionSlotObservedHeld { record: r } => [r]
          SessionSlotObservedUnreadable { line: _ } => []
          SessionSlotObservedAbsent => []
        }),
        unreadable: flat_map(observed, o => match o {
          SessionSlotObservedUnreadable { line: l } => [l]
          SessionSlotObservedHeld { record: _ } => []
          SessionSlotObservedAbsent => []
        }),
      }
    }
    AttemptSlotKeysRefused { detail: d } => SessionSlotRecordsRefused { detail: join(["the session slot store: ", d], "") }
    // ABSENCE IS A CENSUS ANSWER, NOT A SETTLEMENT OR A RECORD. The census proved this store's own
    // directory was never created; the honest answer is that NO slot record is claimed, reported as a
    // refusal so the serve surface cannot render "no attempts" as though it had read an empty store.
    // The constructor is the one this site already used for a listing failure, so nothing moves on an
    // existing route -- only the named fact in the detail changes.
    AttemptSlotKeysAbsent { store: _ } => SessionSlotRecordsRefused { detail: "the session slot store's own directory was never created; the census proves there is no attempt-slot key to read, and no record is claimed" }
  }
}

// THE PASS TAKES THE UNIT OBSERVATIONS AS A FUNCTION OF THE UNIT NAME so a witness can plant them;
// production passes session_worker_unit_lifecycle_for_instance, the worker's own read (unit, then its
// exit record).
fn session_placement_settle_pass_at(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, lifecycle_of: fn(NonEmptyStr) -> UnitLifecycle, now: EpochSecs) -> SessionSettlePass {
  match attempt_slot_keys(store: stores.slots.slots) {
    AttemptSlotKeysListed { keys } => session_settle_keys(stores: stores, host: host, keys: keys, lifecycle_of: lifecycle_of, now: now)
    AttemptSlotKeysRefused { detail: d } => SessionSettlePassRefused { detail: join(["the session slot store: ", d], "") }
    // THE SETTLE PASS IS THE RELEASE ROUTE, SO A CENSUS ANSWER MUST NEVER ACTIVATE IT. A store whose
    // directory was never created answers as a refusal here, exactly as an unreadable store did: the
    // pass reports NOTHING SETTLED and says the store was absent. Reporting
    // SessionSettlePassRan { settlements: [] } would record "I never looked" as "everything settled",
    // which is hold_recovered_by_age_not_observed_holder_death on new substrate. Same constructor as
    // the refused arm, so no existing route moves.
    AttemptSlotKeysAbsent { store: _ } => SessionSettlePassRefused { detail: "the session slot store's own directory was never created; a census answer is never a settlement pass, so nothing is settled and nothing is released" }
  }
}

// ONE READ OF THE CAPACITY PARTITION FOR THE WHOLE PASS. The pass lists K slot keys and every one of them may
// need the charge's fate; reading the partition per key is K reads and K walks of one partition, which is a
// cost-shape defect gunbc.design_argument::earliest_unjustified_boundary fixes regardless of how small K is today, and gunbc.design_argument::minimize_redundancy's answer to it is to share
// the first value. So the partition is read and walked once into a per-reference reading (gunbc.compute.host_capacity
// compute_seat_charge_scans) and each key is answered from that reading by lookup. A partition that cannot be
// read yields one refusal that every key shares, so no two keys can disagree about whether the history was read.
fn session_settle_keys(stores: SessionPlacementStores, host: String, keys: List<NonEmptyStr>, lifecycle_of: fn(NonEmptyStr) -> UnitLifecycle, now: EpochSecs) -> SessionSettlePass {
  let charges = compute_seat_charge_scans(store: stores.store, partition: stores.partition)
  SessionSettlePassRan { settlements: map(keys, k => session_settle_one(stores: stores, host: host, key: k, lifecycle: lifecycle_of(k), now: now, charge: seat_charge_of_scan(reading: charges, reference: k))) }
}

fn session_placement_settle_pass(instance: HostDashboardInstance, stores: SessionPlacementStores) -> SessionSettlePass {
  match now_epoch_seconds() {
    Absent => SessionSettlePassRefused { detail: "the host clock could not be read as epoch seconds, and the reserved-state trigger compares against a deadline" }
    Present { value: now } => session_placement_settle_pass_at(stores: stores, host: instance.host_identity as String, lifecycle_of: u => session_worker_unit_lifecycle_for_instance(instance: instance, unit: u), now: now)
  }
}
